COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.reporting_cadence IS 'The frequency at which this KPI should be measured and reported. Determines the monitoring and optimization cycle for this metric.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.revision_reason IS 'Business justification for the most recent revision to this KPI target. Captures why the target was changed mid-campaign.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.stretch_target_value IS 'The aspirational or stretch goal value for this KPI. Represents exceptional performance beyond the standard target.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.target_audience_segment IS 'The specific audience segment for which this KPI target applies. Allows for segment-specific performance targets within a single campaign.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.target_period IS 'The time period over which the target should be achieved. ''Total'' indicates the target is for the entire campaign/flight/line_item duration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.target_revision_number IS 'Version number tracking revisions to this KPI target. Increments each time the target is modified during campaign execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.target_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the KPI target. Tracks whether the target is in planning, actively being measured, or has been completed or cancelled.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.target_unit IS 'The unit of measure for the target_value. Defines how the target should be interpreted (absolute count, percentage, currency amount, or rating point).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.target_value IS 'The numeric target value for the KPI. Interpretation depends on kpi_type and target_unit (e.g., 1000000 impressions, 2.5% CTR, $50 CPA).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.campaign_kpi_target.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE campaign.flight IS 'Represents a discrete time-bounded execution window within a campaign — a campaign flight (also called a campaign burst or wave). Captures flight name, parent campaign reference, flight start date, flight end date, flight status, flight budget allocation, flight objective override, pacing type (even, front-loaded, back-loaded, custom), pacing goal, daypart restrictions, flight priority, channel mix for this flight, and notes. Enables multi-flight campaign structures where a single campaign runs in sequential or overlapping bursts with distinct budgets and targeting parameters. Aligns with Mediaocean Prisma flight-level planning constructs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.flight_id IS 'Unique identifier for the campaign flight. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign under which this flight executes. Links this flight to its overarching campaign strategy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Individual flights within a campaign can be funded by different cost centers (e.g., different business units or regions). Advertising agencies routinely assign flights to cost centers for sub-campaign LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: A flight''s authorized spend and delivery parameters are governed by a specific Media Insertion Order. Billing reconciliation, pacing oversight, and delivery reporting all require tracing which IO fund';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.milestone_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.milestone. Business justification: Campaign flight launch and completion dates are contractual project milestones (often billing triggers). Linking flight to project_milestone enables integrated timeline management where campaign opera LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.milestone.milestone_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Flights may contract flight-specific suppliers for verification, brand safety, or measurement services. Required for flight-level vendor cost allocation, reconciliation, and performance evaluation in';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.audience_segments IS 'Comma-separated list or structured description of audience segments targeted in this flight (e.g., demographic, behavioral, contextual, or custom segments from DMP/CDP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.budget_allocated IS 'The total budget allocated to this flight, representing the financial envelope for all media buys, creative production, and execution costs within this burst period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.budget_currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the flight budget (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.channel_mix IS 'Comma-separated list or structured description of the media channels included in this flight (e.g., ''Display, Video, Social, OOH''). Defines the multi-channel execution strategy for this burst.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.creative_rotation IS 'The strategy for rotating multiple creatives within this flight (even = equal distribution, weighted = custom weights, optimized = algorithm-driven, sequential = fixed order).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.daypart_restrictions IS 'Time-of-day or day-of-week restrictions for ad delivery within this flight (e.g., ''Weekdays 6AM-10PM'', ''Prime Time Only''). Enables dayparting strategies to optimize audience reach.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.device_targeting IS 'Device types targeted for ad delivery in this flight (e.g., ''Desktop, Mobile, Tablet, CTV''). Enables cross-device or device-specific strategies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.end_date IS 'The date when this flight concludes execution. Marks the end of the time-bounded burst window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.flight_code IS 'Externally-known unique code or identifier for this flight, used in trafficking systems, insertion orders, and billing reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.flight_name IS 'Human-readable name or label for this flight, often indicating the burst period, theme, or seasonal focus (e.g., ''Holiday Wave 1'', ''Back-to-School Burst'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.flight_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the flight. Indicates whether the flight is in planning, actively running, paused, or concluded.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.frequency_cap IS 'Maximum number of times a single user should see an ad from this flight within a defined time window. Prevents ad fatigue and optimizes budget efficiency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.frequency_cap_period IS 'The time window over which the frequency cap is enforced (e.g., per day, per week, for the entire flight duration).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.geo_targeting IS 'Geographic targeting parameters for this flight, specifying countries, regions, DMAs, postal codes, or custom geo-fences where ads should be delivered.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.notes IS 'Free-text notes or comments about this flight, capturing special instructions, strategic rationale, or operational considerations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.objective IS 'The primary marketing objective for this flight. May override or refine the parent campaign objective for this specific burst period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.pacing_goal IS 'The metric by which pacing is measured and controlled (e.g., impressions delivered, clicks generated, conversions achieved, unique reach, or spend amount).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.pacing_type IS 'The budget pacing strategy for this flight. Determines how spend is distributed across the flight duration (even = uniform daily spend, front_loaded = higher spend at start, back_loaded = higher spend at end, custom = user-defined schedule).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.priority IS 'Numeric priority ranking for this flight relative to other flights in the same campaign or portfolio. Higher values indicate higher priority for budget allocation and inventory access.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.start_date IS 'The date when this flight begins execution. Marks the start of the time-bounded burst window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.target_frequency IS 'The planned average number of times each unique user should be exposed to the ad during this flight. Used to balance reach and repetition.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.target_grp IS 'The planned Gross Rating Points for this flight, representing the sum of all rating points delivered. Standard metric for traditional media planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.target_impressions IS 'The planned number of ad impressions to be delivered during this flight. Used for pacing and performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.target_reach IS 'The planned number of unique individuals or households to be reached during this flight. Key metric for awareness campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.target_trp IS 'The planned Target Rating Points for this flight, representing GRP adjusted for the specific target audience. Used for audience-specific media planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.flight.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE campaign.pacing_rule IS 'Defines the delivery pacing strategy and guardrails for a campaign, flight, or line item. Captures pacing rule name, parent entity type, parent entity reference, pacing type (even, accelerated, front-loaded, back-loaded, custom curve), daily impression goal, daily spend cap, weekly impression goal, weekly spend cap, pacing check frequency (hourly, daily), over-delivery action (pause, throttle, alert), under-delivery action (boost, alert), pacing alert threshold percentage, auto-optimization enabled flag, optimization algorithm reference, and effective date range. Governs how campaign delivery is distributed over time to meet KPIs and avoid over/under-spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.pacing_rule_id IS 'Unique identifier for the pacing rule record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign entity to which this pacing rule applies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.flight_id IS 'Reference to the parent flight entity to which this pacing rule applies, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.line_item_id IS 'Reference to the parent line item entity to which this pacing rule applies, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.auto_optimization_enabled IS 'Indicates whether automated optimization algorithms are enabled to adjust pacing dynamically based on performance data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary values in this pacing rule (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.custom_curve_definition IS 'JSON or structured definition of a custom pacing curve when pacing_type is set to custom_curve. Defines delivery distribution over time.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.daily_impression_goal IS 'Target number of impressions to be delivered per day under this pacing rule.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.daily_spend_cap IS 'Maximum spend allowed per day under this pacing rule, expressed in the campaign currency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.dayparting_enabled IS 'Indicates whether dayparting (time-of-day targeting) is applied as part of the pacing strategy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.dayparting_schedule IS 'Structured definition of the dayparting schedule (e.g., JSON or cron-like format) specifying hours and days when delivery is allowed or prioritized.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.effective_end_date IS 'The date on which this pacing rule ceases to be active. Null indicates an open-ended rule.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.effective_start_date IS 'The date from which this pacing rule becomes active and begins governing delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.notes IS 'Free-text notes or comments about this pacing rule, used for documentation and operational context.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.over_delivery_action IS 'The action to be taken when delivery exceeds the pacing goal or cap (e.g., pause delivery, throttle impressions, send alert).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.pacing_alert_threshold_pct IS 'The percentage deviation from the pacing goal that triggers an alert to campaign managers (e.g., 10.00 means alert if delivery is 10% off target).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.pacing_check_frequency IS 'The frequency at which the pacing engine evaluates delivery progress against goals and applies throttling or boosting actions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.pacing_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the pacing rule indicating whether it is actively governing delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.pacing_type IS 'The delivery pacing strategy applied to the campaign or line item. Defines how impressions or spend are distributed over the flight period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.parent_entity_type IS 'The type of parent entity to which this pacing rule is attached (e.g., campaign, flight, line item, insertion order).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.priority_level IS 'Numeric priority level for this pacing rule when multiple rules apply to the same entity. Higher values indicate higher priority.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.rule_name IS 'Human-readable name or label for the pacing rule, used for identification and reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.timezone IS 'IANA timezone identifier (e.g., America/New_York, Europe/London) used for interpreting pacing schedules and dayparting rules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.under_delivery_action IS 'The action to be taken when delivery falls short of the pacing goal (e.g., boost bid, send alert, reallocate budget).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.weekly_impression_goal IS 'Target number of impressions to be delivered per week under this pacing rule.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.weekly_spend_cap IS 'Maximum spend allowed per week under this pacing rule, expressed in the campaign currency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.pacing_rule.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE campaign.targeting_rule IS 'Defines the audience, contextual, and brand safety targeting parameters applied to a campaign, flight, or line item. Captures targeting rule name, parent entity type (campaign/flight/line_item), parent entity reference, targeting dimension (geography, demographic, behavioral, contextual, keyword, device, daypart, audience segment, retargeting, lookalike, brand_safety_content_exclusion, brand_safety_keyword_block, brand_safety_domain_block, brand_safety_category_exclusion), targeting operator (include/exclude), targeting value, targeting value type, data source (first-party, second-party, third-party, DMP, CDP), audience segment reference, geo level (country, region, DMA, city, postal code), device type, OS type, browser type, connection type, language, daypart schedule, frequency cap limit, frequency cap window, frequency cap unit, brand safety tier (TAG certified, GARM standard), viewability standard, fraud prevention threshold, GDPR consent required flag, CCPA opt-out flag, recency window, and is_active flag. Enables precise audience targeting governance and brand safety enforcement across programmatic and direct channels.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.targeting_rule_id IS 'Unique identifier for the targeting rule. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.campaign_id IS 'The identifier of the parent entity (campaign, flight, or line_item) to which this targeting rule applies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: targeting_rule has parent_entity_type attribute indicating it can apply to campaign, flight, or line_item. Currently only has campaign_id FK. Adding flight_id (nullable) to support flight-level target';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: targeting_rule has parent_entity_type attribute indicating it can apply to campaign, flight, or line_item. Currently only has campaign_id FK. Adding line_item_id (nullable) to support line_item-level';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.segment_id IS 'Reference to the audience segment when targeting dimension is audience_segment, retargeting, or lookalike. LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.brand_safety_tier IS 'The brand safety standard applied: Trustworthy Accountability Group (TAG) certified, Global Alliance for Responsible Media (GARM) standard, or custom.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.browser_type IS 'The web browser targeted (e.g., Chrome, Safari, Firefox, Edge).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.ccpa_opt_out_flag IS 'Indicates whether this targeting rule respects CCPA opt-out requests (Do Not Sell My Personal Information).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.connection_type IS 'The type of network connection targeted: WiFi, cellular, ethernet, or unknown.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.data_source IS 'The origin of the targeting data: first-party (owned), second-party (partner), third-party (purchased), Data Management Platform (DMP), or Customer Data Platform (CDP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.daypart_schedule IS 'The time-of-day or day-of-week schedule for ad delivery, specified in a structured format (e.g., JSON or cron-like expression).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.device_type IS 'The type of device targeted: desktop, mobile, tablet, Connected TV (CTV), Over-the-Top (OTT), or wearable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.effective_end_date IS 'The date when this targeting rule expires and is no longer applied. Null indicates no expiration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.effective_start_date IS 'The date when this targeting rule becomes active and begins to be applied.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.fraud_prevention_threshold IS 'The minimum fraud detection score (0-100) required for ad delivery, used to filter out suspected invalid traffic.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.frequency_cap_limit IS 'The maximum number of times an ad can be shown to a user within the specified frequency cap window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.frequency_cap_unit IS 'The time unit for the frequency cap window: hour, day, week, month, or lifetime.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.frequency_cap_window IS 'The time window (in the unit specified by frequency_cap_unit) over which the frequency cap limit applies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.gdpr_consent_required IS 'Indicates whether GDPR user consent is required for this targeting rule to be applied.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.geo_level IS 'The granularity of geographic targeting: country, region/state, Designated Market Area (DMA), city, or postal code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.is_active IS 'Indicates whether this targeting rule is currently active and being applied to ad delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.language IS 'The language targeted, specified as ISO 639-1 two-letter language code (e.g., en, es, fr).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.os_type IS 'The operating system targeted (e.g., iOS, Android, Windows, macOS, tvOS).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.parent_entity_type IS 'The type of entity to which this targeting rule is applied: campaign, flight, or line_item.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.priority IS 'The priority or precedence of this targeting rule when multiple rules apply to the same entity. Lower numbers indicate higher priority.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.recency_window IS 'The time window (in days) for behavioral or retargeting data recency, specifying how recent user activity must be to qualify for targeting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.rule_name IS 'Business-friendly name for the targeting rule, used for identification and reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.targeting_dimension IS 'The dimension or category of targeting applied by this rule. Code set: ref.targeting_dimension.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.targeting_operator IS 'Specifies whether the targeting rule includes or excludes the specified targeting value.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.targeting_value IS 'The specific value or identifier for the targeting dimension (e.g., country code, age range, device type, audience segment ID).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.targeting_value_type IS 'Indicates the format of the targeting value: single value, range, comma-separated list, or pattern/regex.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.viewability_standard IS 'The viewability measurement standard applied: Media Rating Council (MRC), Interactive Advertising Bureau (IAB), or custom.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.targeting_rule.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE campaign.ad IS 'Individual ad unit record representing a specific creative execution trafficked and served within a campaign line item. Captures ad name, parent line item reference, campaign reference, ad type (banner, video, native, rich media, audio, DOOH), ad format dimensions (width x height), VAST/VPAID tag reference, click-through URL, impression tracker URL, view tracker URL, creative asset reference, ad status (draft, pending review, approved, rejected, live, paused, archived), trafficking status, ad server ad ID (CM360), go-live date, end date, frequency cap, frequency cap period, and audit timestamps. Bridges the campaign execution layer to the creative asset layer. Aligns with Google Campaign Manager 360 ad trafficking entities.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.ad_id IS 'Unique identifier for the ad unit. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.asset_id IS 'Reference to the creative asset (image, video, HTML5, audio) used in this ad execution. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign to which this ad belongs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.creative_assignment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.creative_assignment. Business justification: An ad unit is the trafficked execution of a creative assignment — it represents the specific creative asset assigned to a line item being served. Adding creative_assignment_id to ad creates a direct,';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: An ad is executed within a flight''s time window and targeting context. While flight can be derived via ad → line_item → flight, a direct flight_id on ad is operationally valuable for ad-server pacing,';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.line_item_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign line item under which this ad is trafficked.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.media_placement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_placement. Business justification: An ad runs within a specific contracted media placement (inventory slot on a publisher property). Delivery verification, viewability measurement, and brand safety compliance reporting all require know';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Each ad unit must conform to a technical spec (file format, dimensions, duration, VAST requirements) for its placement. Ad servers validate ads against specs before trafficking go-live. This link enab LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.spec.spec_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Individual ads may use specific suppliers for dynamic creative optimization, ad serving, or verification services. Required for ad-level vendor cost tracking, performance attribution, and troubleshoot';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Ad serving and third-party tracking assignment: each ad is delivered via a specific tech partner (ad server/verification vendor). ad carries vast_tag_url, vpaid_enabled, third_party_tracking_enabled,';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.trafficking_instruction_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.trafficking_instruction. Business justification: Each ad unit is governed by a trafficking instruction specifying ad-server tags, pixels, VAST URLs, and targeting directives. Ad ops teams must link ads to their trafficking instructions for ad-server';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.trafficking_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.trafficking_order. Business justification: Ads are trafficked to ad servers via trafficking orders. Currently no FK exists to track which trafficking order activated a specific ad. This is essential for operational tracking (when was this ad t';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.ad_name IS 'Human-readable name assigned to this ad unit for identification and reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.ad_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the ad unit. Governs whether the ad is eligible for serving. Code set: ref.ad_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.ad_type IS 'Classification of the ad unit by format type. Determines rendering and trafficking requirements. Code set: ref.ad_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.approval_date IS 'Date when the ad was approved for trafficking and serving.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the user who approved the ad for serving.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.brand_safety_verified IS 'Indicates whether the ad creative has passed brand safety verification checks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.ccpa_opt_out_honored IS 'Indicates whether this ad honors CCPA Do Not Sell requests.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.click_through_url IS 'Destination URL where users are directed when they click on the ad. May include tracking macros.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.end_date IS 'Date when the ad stops serving. Null indicates no end date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.format IS 'Dimensions of the ad creative in width x height format (e.g., 300x250, 728x90, 1920x1080). Null for non-display formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.frequency_cap IS 'Maximum number of times this ad can be shown to a unique user within the frequency cap period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.frequency_cap_period IS 'Time window over which the frequency cap is enforced.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.gdpr_consent_required IS 'Indicates whether user consent is required under GDPR before serving this ad.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.go_live_date IS 'Date when the ad becomes eligible to start serving.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.impression_tracker_url IS 'Third-party tracking pixel or beacon URL fired when the ad impression is served.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.landing_page_url IS 'Final destination landing page URL after click-through, excluding tracking parameters.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.notes IS 'Free-text notes or comments about the ad unit for internal reference and collaboration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.priority IS 'Serving priority of this ad relative to other ads in the same line item. Higher values indicate higher priority.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.rejection_reason IS 'Explanation for why the ad was rejected during review. Null if not rejected.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.server_ad_code IS 'External identifier assigned by the ad server platform (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360) for this ad unit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.ssl_compliant IS 'Indicates whether the ad creative and all tracking tags are served over HTTPS for secure delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.third_party_tracking_enabled IS 'Indicates whether third-party tracking pixels and beacons are enabled for this ad.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.trafficking_status IS 'Operational status indicating whether the ad has been trafficked to the ad server and its current serving state.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.vast_tag_url IS 'VAST or VPAID tag URL for video ad serving. Null for non-video ad types.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.view_tracker_url IS 'Third-party tracking URL fired when the ad is viewable according to MRC viewability standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.vpaid_enabled IS 'Indicates whether the ad uses VPAID for interactive video ad execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.weight IS 'Relative weight for rotation when multiple ads are eligible to serve. Used for A/B testing and creative rotation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.ad.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE campaign.creative_assignment IS 'This association product represents the assignment of creative assets to line items for media execution. It captures the operational relationship between what is being bought (line item) and what creative content is served (creative asset). Each record links one line item to one creative asset with attributes that govern rotation, scheduling, trafficking, and performance tracking for that specific pairing.. Existence Justification: In advertising operations, line items routinely serve multiple creative assets simultaneously through rotation strategies (A/B testing, dynamic creative optimization, sequential messaging). Each creative asset is reused across multiple line items spanning different campaigns, flights, and targeting strategies. The business actively manages creative assignments as operational records with rotation weights, scheduling windows, trafficking status, and performance metrics tracked per line-item-asset pairing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.creative_assignment_id IS 'Unique identifier for this creative assignment record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.asset_id IS 'Foreign key linking to the creative asset assigned to this line item LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.deliverable_tracker_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.deliverable_tracker. Business justification: A creative assignment (assigning a produced asset to a line item) is the downstream outcome of a creative production deliverable. Linking enables agencies to trace from project deliverable through to LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.deliverable_tracker.deliverable_tracker_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to the line item that will serve this creative asset';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.media_placement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_placement. Business justification: A creative assignment maps a creative asset to a specific media placement for delivery. Placement-level creative performance reporting and brand safety verification per placement require this direct l';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.click_count IS 'The number of clicks generated by this specific creative asset on this specific line item. Performance metric tracked at the assignment level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.conversion_count IS 'The number of conversions attributed to this specific creative asset on this specific line item. Performance metric for conversion-based campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.ctr IS 'Click-through rate for this creative-line item pairing, calculated as (clicks / impressions). Performance metric for creative effectiveness.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.end_date IS 'The date when this creative asset stops serving on this line item. Supports flight-based creative strategies and seasonal messaging.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.impression_count IS 'The number of impressions delivered for this specific creative asset on this specific line item. Performance metric tracked at the assignment level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.priority_rank IS 'The priority or sequence order of this creative within the line item''s rotation. Used when rotation is not purely weight-based but follows a priority waterfall.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.rotation_weight IS 'The percentage or weight assigned to this creative asset within the line item''s creative rotation. Used for A/B testing and dynamic creative optimization. Sum of weights across all assignments for a line item typically equals 100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.start_date IS 'The date when this creative asset begins serving on this line item. Enables sequential messaging and time-based creative rotation strategies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.trafficking_status IS 'The operational status of this specific creative-to-line-item assignment in the ad serving platform. Indicates whether the creative has been successfully trafficked and is ready to serve.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.view_count IS 'The number of video views or viewable impressions for this specific creative asset on this specific line item. Applicable to video and viewability-measured formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: assignment_created_date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.creative_assignment.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE campaign.line_item IS 'Granular execution unit within a campaign flight representing a single buyable unit of media — the atomic record of what is being bought, at what price, on which channel, for which audience. Captures line item name, parent flight reference, campaign reference, channel type (display, video, search, social, OOH, CTV, audio), ad format, placement type, targeting summary, start date, end date, booked impressions, booked clicks, booked views, rate type (CPM, CPC, CPA, CPV, flat), rate amount, net cost, gross cost, currency, IO reference, vendor/publisher reference, trafficking status, delivery status, pacing status, and creative assignment status. The primary unit of media planning and buying execution. Aligns with Google Campaign Manager 360 placement and The Trade Desk ad group constructs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.line_item_id IS 'Unique identifier for the line item. Primary key for the line item execution unit within a campaign flight.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign under which this line item executes. Enables rollup reporting and budget tracking at campaign level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: Line items are priced per contracted rate cards. Direct FK enables rate compliance reporting — verifying line_item rate_amount matches the contracted rate card — and supports billing audits. Advertisi LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.creative_brief_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_brief. Business justification: Media planners link line items to creative briefs to ensure each placement''s creative requirements (format, messaging, channel) are fulfilled. This traceability is essential for creative-to-media alig LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.creative_brief.creative_brief_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.creative_deliverable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_deliverable. Business justification: Line items require specific creative deliverables (banner sizes, video lengths) to be produced and trafficked. Linking line items to deliverables enables production-to-media readiness tracking — a nam LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.creative_deliverable.creative_deliverable_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.flight_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign flight that contains this line item. Establishes the hierarchical relationship between flight and line item.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: A line item''s booked spend is authorized by a Media Insertion Order. Finance reconciliation, billing, and delivery reporting require tracing each line item to its governing IO. The existing contract_i';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.plan_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan_line. Business justification: A line item is the execution-layer realization of a media plan line. Plan-vs-actual delivery reporting — a core media accountability process — requires linking each executed line item back to the plan';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.programmatic_deal_id IS 'The unique identifier for a programmatic deal (PMP, preferred deal, or programmatic guaranteed) associated with this line item. Nullable for open exchange buys.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Line items define placement requirements (ad format, dimensions, IAB unit) that must match a creative spec. Trafficking teams validate assigned creatives against the line item''s spec before go-live. T LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.spec.spec_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Line items frequently use suppliers beyond publishers (ad verification, measurement partners, data providers). Critical for line-item-level vendor reconciliation, cost attribution, and compliance trac';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.trafficking_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.trafficking_order. Business justification: Line items are trafficked to ad servers via trafficking orders. Currently no FK exists to track which trafficking order activated a specific line item. This is essential for operational tracking and a';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.vendor_publisher_id IS 'Reference to the media vendor or publisher delivering this line item inventory. Links to vendor master for billing and performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: In advertising agencies, each line item''s production and trafficking execution is managed as a work package. Linking enables project managers to track effort, cost, and status per media buy — essentia LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.work_package.work_package_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.ad_format IS 'The creative format specification for this line item (e.g., 300x250 banner, 15-second pre-roll, sponsored post). Defines the deliverable unit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.agency_commission_rate IS 'The commission percentage applied to this line item. Expressed as a percentage (e.g., 15.00 for 15%). Used to calculate net from gross cost.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.booked_clicks IS 'The contracted number of clicks to be delivered for this line item. Primary delivery goal for click-based buys.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.booked_conversions IS 'The contracted number of conversions or acquisitions to be delivered for this line item. Primary delivery goal for performance-based buys.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.booked_impressions IS 'The contracted number of impressions to be delivered for this line item. Primary delivery goal for impression-based buys.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.booked_views IS 'The contracted number of video views or viewable impressions to be delivered for this line item. Primary delivery goal for video and viewability-based buys.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.brand_safety_tier IS 'The level of brand safety filtering applied to this line item. Determines which content categories and contexts are excluded.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.channel_type IS 'The media channel through which this line item will be executed. Determines platform, format options, and measurement methodology. Code set: ref.channel_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.creative_assignment_status IS 'The status of creative asset assignment and approval for this line item. Indicates whether creatives are ready for serving.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary values on this line item. Enables multi-currency campaign management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.delivery_status IS 'The current delivery performance status of the line item. Indicates whether the line item is meeting, exceeding, or falling short of delivery goals. Code set: ref.delivery_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.end_date IS 'The date when this line item stops serving. Defines the end of the delivery window. Nullable for evergreen line items.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.frequency_cap_impressions IS 'The maximum number of impressions a unique user can receive for this line item within the frequency cap period. Used to control ad exposure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.frequency_cap_period IS 'The time period over which the frequency cap is applied. Defines the window for impression counting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.gross_cost IS 'The gross media cost for this line item before agency commission. Represents the total amount billed to the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.is_programmatic IS 'Indicates whether this line item is executed through programmatic buying platforms (DSP) or through direct/manual insertion orders.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.line_item_code IS 'External business identifier or SKU for the line item. Used for trafficking, billing reconciliation, and cross-system reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.line_item_name IS 'Human-readable name for the line item. Typically includes targeting, format, and channel descriptors for operational clarity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.line_sequence IS 'Ordinal position of this line item within the parent flight. Used for display ordering and operational sequencing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.net_cost IS 'The net media cost for this line item after agency commission and discounts. Used for internal P&L and margin analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.pacing_status IS 'The current pacing health of the line item relative to its delivery goal and timeline. Used for proactive delivery management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.pacing_strategy IS 'The delivery pacing strategy for this line item. Determines how impressions are distributed across the flight period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.placement_type IS 'The buying model or inventory type for this line item. Indicates whether inventory is reserved, auction-based, or programmatic. Code set: ref.placement_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.priority IS 'The delivery priority of this line item relative to other line items competing for the same inventory. Higher values indicate higher priority.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.rate_amount IS 'The unit rate for this line item based on the rate type. For CPM, this is cost per thousand impressions; for CPC, cost per click; for flat, total cost.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.rate_type IS 'The pricing model for this line item. Determines how cost is calculated based on delivery metrics (Cost Per Mille, Cost Per Click, Cost Per Acquisition, Cost Per View, flat fee). Code set: ref.rate_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.start_date IS 'The date when this line item begins serving. Defines the start of the delivery window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.targeting_summary IS 'High-level summary of audience targeting parameters applied to this line item (demographics, geography, behavior, context). Detailed targeting stored in related tables.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.trafficking_status IS 'The operational status of line item setup and creative trafficking. Indicates readiness for delivery. Code set: ref.trafficking_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.viewability_target_percentage IS 'The target percentage of impressions that must meet viewability standards (MRC definition: 50% of pixels in view for 1 second for display, 2 seconds for video).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.line_item.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE campaign.trafficking_order IS 'Represents the formal trafficking instruction set issued to an ad server or DSP to activate campaign line items and ads. Captures trafficking order number, parent campaign reference, parent flight reference, ad server platform (CM360, The Trade Desk, etc.), trafficking status (pending, submitted, in-progress, live, completed, rejected), submitted by, submitted date, go-live date, trafficking notes, QA status, QA completed by, QA completed date, number of line items trafficked, number of ads trafficked, VAST tag validation status, pixel firing validation status, and audit timestamps. Represents the operational handoff from planning to execution — a distinct business workflow from the campaign plan itself.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.trafficking_order_id IS 'Unique identifier for the trafficking order. Primary key for the trafficking order entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign for which this trafficking order is issued.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Trafficking orders execute the media buys authorized by insertion orders. Direct FK enables IO-level trafficking status reporting and billing reconciliation — ''which IO does this trafficking order ful LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.flight_id IS 'Reference to the parent flight or media schedule within the campaign that this trafficking order activates.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.parent_trafficking_order_id IS 'Reference to the original trafficking order if this is a revision or amendment, enabling tracking of the full order history and change lineage.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Trafficking orders involve third-party ad servers or trafficking platforms (suppliers). Essential for tracking which ad server/platform was used, critical for troubleshooting, billing, and vendor perf';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.task_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.task. Business justification: Trafficking orders are executed as project tasks with SLA commitments. Linking enables project managers to track trafficking task completion against campaign go-live dates, measure SLA adherence, and LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.task.task_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Trafficking orders are submitted to a specific ad server platform (tech partner). trafficking_order.ad_server_platform is a denormalized string identifying the tech partner; replacing it with a proper';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.trafficking_instruction_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.trafficking_instruction. Business justification: A trafficking order (internal workflow) generates trafficking instructions (ad-server directives). Linking them enables end-to-end trafficking workflow tracking: from internal order creation through a';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.actual_live_timestamp IS 'Actual date and time when the trafficking order went live and ads began serving, as confirmed by the ad server platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.ad_server_order_code IS 'External order or campaign identifier assigned by the ad server platform (e.g., CM360 order ID, Trade Desk campaign ID) for cross-system reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.ads_trafficked_count IS 'Total number of individual ad creatives that were trafficked and uploaded to the ad server as part of this trafficking order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.completion_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the trafficking order was marked as completed, indicating that all line items and ads are live and the operational handoff is finalized.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.go_live_date IS 'Scheduled date when the trafficked campaign line items and ads are expected to begin serving live impressions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.line_items_trafficked_count IS 'Total number of campaign line items that were trafficked and configured in the ad server as part of this trafficking order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.pixel_firing_validation_status IS 'Validation status of tracking pixels and conversion tags, confirming that impression, click, and conversion pixels are firing correctly in test environments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.priority_level IS 'Operational priority assigned to this trafficking order, indicating urgency and sequencing for ad operations team workload management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.qa_completed_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the quality assurance review was completed and the trafficking order was approved or rejected for go-live.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.qa_status IS 'Current status of the quality assurance review process for this trafficking order, indicating whether pre-launch validation checks have been completed and passed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.rejection_reason IS 'Detailed explanation provided when a trafficking order is rejected during QA or by the ad server platform, including specific issues that must be resolved before resubmission.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.revision_number IS 'Sequential version number tracking revisions and resubmissions of the trafficking order due to changes, corrections, or rejections.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.sla_met_flag IS 'Boolean indicator of whether the trafficking order was completed within the defined SLA target hours, used for operational performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.sla_target_hours IS 'Target number of hours within which the trafficking order should be completed from submission to go-live, as defined by internal SLA policies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.submitted_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the trafficking order was submitted to the ad server or DSP for processing and activation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.trafficking_notes IS 'Free-text operational notes and instructions provided by the trafficking team regarding special setup requirements, targeting parameters, creative specifications, or platform-specific configurations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.trafficking_order_number IS 'Business-facing unique trafficking order number used for operational reference and communication with ad ops teams and external platforms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.trafficking_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the trafficking order indicating its progress through the ad operations workflow from submission to go-live. Code set: ref.trafficking_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.trafficking_type IS 'Classification of the trafficking order based on the campaign buying model and activation method (standard direct IO, programmatic guaranteed, sponsorship, etc.).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.vast_tag_validation_status IS 'Validation status of VAST tags for video ad creatives, indicating whether the tags conform to IAB VAST specifications and are ready for serving.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN campaign.trafficking_order.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.media_placement IS 'Operational record representing a specific ad placement purchased from a media vendor — the atomic unit of a media buy. Captures placement name, ad unit size/format, channel type, vendor/publisher, site/station/network, position, targeting parameters, flight start/end dates, contracted units, contracted impressions, rate type (CPM, CPC, CPA, flat), contracted rate, total contracted value, trafficking status, and ad server placement ID from Google Campaign Manager 360. Links to insertion order and media plan line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.media_placement_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the media placement record. This is the atomic unit of a media buy, representing a specific ad placement purchased from a media vendor. Role: TRANSACTION_LINE.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: placement defines specific ad placement positions within a publisher property and channel. Currently placement has no FK to ad_channel. This FK establishes that each placement operates within a specif';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.ad_format_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_format. Business justification: media_placement currently has ad_format and ad_unit_size as STRING attributes. Each placement is for a specific ad format (e.g., 300x250 Banner, Pre-roll Video). This FK normalizes the placement-to-fo';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.ad_server_tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Media placements reference ad_server_platform as plain text. Linking to tech_partner normalizes this and enables ad serving vendor management: tracking tech fees per placement, SLA compliance for ad s';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.asset_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.asset. Business justification: Placements are assigned specific creative assets for delivery. Essential for trafficking, ad server setup, and ensuring creative specs match placement requirements. Distinct from ad_server_placement_i LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: Media placements carry contracted_rate and contracted_value fields that must be validated against the negotiated rate card. This link enables placement-level rate compliance auditing — verifying that LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Media placements incur contracted costs that require cost center attribution for financial reporting. Placement-level cost center coding supports granular P&L analysis by channel and client, and is re LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Placements are the billing unit for media reconciliation. GL account coding at placement level supports invoice line matching, accrual posting, and billing dispute resolution. Agency billing systems r LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.media_ad_server_placement_id IS 'The placement identifier assigned by Google Campaign Manager 360 (CM360) ad server used for trafficking, creative assignment, and delivery reporting. This is the operational key used by ad operations teams to manage the placement in the ad server.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.media_catalog_placement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.placement. Business justification: media_placement is the operational purchased placement record, while placement is the catalog/reference definition of a placement position. An operational media_placement should reference the catalog';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Reference to the parent Insertion Order (IO) under which this placement was purchased. An IO is the binding contract between the advertiser/agency and the media vendor authorizing the placement. Serves as the HEADER_REFERENCE for this transaction line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.original_placement_media_placement_id IS 'For make-good placements (is_makegood = true), the reference to the original media_placement_id that this placement is compensating for. Enables traceability between under-delivered placements and their corresponding make-good replacements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.primary_media_audience_segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Placements are bought and trafficked against specific audience segments. Ad ops teams require explicit segment linkage for ad server targeting setup, delivery pacing, and performance reporting by audi LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.programmatic_deal_id IS 'The unique deal identifier for programmatic private marketplace (PMP) or programmatic guaranteed deals, as assigned by the Supply-Side Platform (SSP) or publisher. Used to activate and track the deal in The Trade Desk Demand-Side Platform (DSP). Null for direct or open auction buys.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.publisher_id IS 'Reference to the media vendor or publisher from whom this placement was purchased (e.g., Google, Meta, NBC Universal, Clear Channel). Serves as the PARTY_REFERENCE for this transaction line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.publisher_property_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.publisher_property. Business justification: placement defines specific ad positions within a publisher property (e.g., homepage leaderboard on NYTimes.com). Each placement belongs to one publisher property. This FK establishes the parent-child';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Ad ops teams must verify that a placement''s accepted ad unit size, format, and technical requirements match the creative spec before trafficking. Placement-to-spec alignment is a mandatory pre-traffic LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.spec.spec_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.above_fold_classification IS 'Classification indicating whether the placement typically appears above or below the fold on initial page load, critical for viewability.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.ad_unit_size IS 'Dimensions of the ad unit in pixels (e.g., 728x90, 300x250, 1920x1080) or duration for video/audio placements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.agency_commission_pct IS 'The agency commission percentage applied to this placement''s gross contracted value, typically 15% per industry standard (4As convention). Used to calculate net media cost billed to the client versus gross cost paid to the vendor. Part of the MONETARY_TRIPLET adjustment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.approved_date IS 'The date on which this placement was formally approved by the client or account team, authorizing the media vendor to proceed with trafficking and delivery. Represents the BUSINESS_EVENT_TIMESTAMP for the placement authorization event.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.brand_safety_category IS 'The IAB content category exclusion or inclusion list applied to this placement to ensure brand-safe ad delivery (e.g., ''Exclude: Adult Content, Violence, Hate Speech''). Configured in Google CM360 or The Trade Desk per TAG Brand Safety standards and client brand guidelines.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.brand_safety_tier IS 'Brand safety classification tier for this placement, indicating content adjacency risk level per Trustworthy Accountability Group (TAG) standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.buying_method IS 'The method by which this placement was purchased: direct IO with publisher, programmatic guaranteed, private marketplace (PMP) deal, open auction Real-Time Bidding (RTB), or preferred deal. Determines the applicable technology stack (e.g., The Trade Desk for programmatic, Mediaocean Prisma for direct).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.cancellation_notice_days IS 'Number of days advance notice required to cancel or modify a booked campaign on this placement without penalty.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.channel_type IS 'The media channel category for this placement (e.g., digital display, broadcast TV, Out-of-Home (OOH), Connected TV (CTV)/Over-the-Top (OTT), print). Drives channel-specific reporting, rate card application, and regulatory compliance requirements. Code set: ref.channel_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.content_category IS 'IAB Content Taxonomy category for the content surrounding this placement (e.g., News, Sports, Entertainment, Finance).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.contracted_impressions IS 'The total number of ad impressions guaranteed or estimated for this placement under the IO. For CPM-based buys this is the primary delivery metric; for GRP/TRP buys this is the estimated impression equivalent. Used for reach/frequency planning and MRC-compliant delivery verification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.contracted_rate IS 'The negotiated unit rate for this placement as agreed in the Insertion Order (IO), expressed in the applicable rate type currency (e.g., CPM rate in USD, CPC rate in USD, flat fee in USD). This is commercially sensitive pricing data. Serves as the LINE_VALUE_OR_RESULT for this transaction line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.contracted_units IS 'The total number of units (impressions, clicks, acquisitions, GRPs, or flat occurrences) contracted for this placement as specified in the Insertion Order. Serves as the LINE_QUANTITY for this transaction line. Used for pacing, delivery tracking, and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.contracted_value IS 'The total gross monetary value of this placement as contracted in the Insertion Order (IO), calculated as contracted rate × contracted units. Represents the full financial commitment for this placement before any adjustments, make-goods, or agency commission. Part of the MONETARY_TRIPLET.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.cpm_floor_price IS 'Minimum CPM rate for this placement position, used in programmatic bidding and rate card negotiations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.cpm_list_price IS 'Published list CPM rate for this placement on the rate card, before negotiation or discounts.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for all monetary values on this placement (e.g., ''USD'', ''GBP'', ''EUR''). Required for multi-currency media buys and financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA. Part of the MONETARY_TRIPLET.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.daypart_availability IS 'Time-of-day availability for this placement (e.g., Prime Time, Daytime, Late Night, Run-of-Schedule), relevant for broadcast and digital video.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.device_targeting IS 'Device type targeting parameters for this placement position.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.effective_end_date IS 'Date when this placement position will be or was retired from available inventory (nullable for ongoing placements).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.effective_start_date IS 'Date when this placement position became available in inventory for booking and trafficking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.environment_type IS 'The platform environment where the placement is delivered (web, mobile app, Connected TV (CTV), Over-the-Top (OTT), Digital Out-of-Home (DOOH), etc.). Code set: ref.environment_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.estimated_monthly_impressions IS 'Projected monthly impression volume available for this placement position, used in media planning and forecasting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.estimated_reach_pct IS 'Estimated percentage of target audience reached by this placement within a standard campaign flight.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.flight_end_date IS 'The date on which the ad placement is scheduled to stop delivering. Defines the end of the placement''s active flight period. Used for campaign scheduling, delivery completion tracking, and IO reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.flight_start_date IS 'The date on which the ad placement is scheduled to begin delivering impressions or airing. Defines the start of the placement''s active flight period. Used for campaign scheduling, pacing calculations, and IO compliance verification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.frequency_cap IS 'The maximum number of times a unique user or household may be served this ad within the defined frequency cap period. Configured in Google CM360 or The Trade Desk to control ad fatigue and optimize reach. Null if no frequency cap is applied.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.frequency_cap_impressions IS 'Maximum number of impressions per user within the frequency cap period, enforced at placement level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.frequency_cap_period IS 'The time window over which the frequency cap applies (e.g., per day, per week, per month, lifetime of the campaign). Works in conjunction with frequency_cap to define the full frequency capping rule in the ad server.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.geo_targeting_scope IS 'Geographic targeting granularity available for this placement (global, national, Designated Market Area (DMA), postal code, etc.).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.grp_contracted IS 'The total Gross Rating Points (GRP) contracted for this placement, applicable to broadcast TV, radio, and OOH buys. GRP = Reach% × Frequency. Used for broadcast media planning, Nielsen audience measurement reconciliation, and post-buy analysis. Null for digital-only placements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.is_guaranteed_inventory IS 'Flag indicating whether this placement is sold as guaranteed inventory (direct buy) versus non-guaranteed (programmatic auction).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.is_makegood IS 'Indicates whether this placement was created as a make-good (compensatory placement) to replace under-delivered or cancelled inventory from a prior placement. Make-goods are tracked separately for financial reconciliation and vendor performance management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.is_programmatic_eligible IS 'Flag indicating whether this placement is available for programmatic buying through Demand-Side Platforms (DSP) and Supply-Side Platforms (SSP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.makegood_policy IS 'Publisher policy for makegoods (compensatory ad delivery) when this placement underdelivers against contracted impressions or performance benchmarks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.net_contracted_value IS 'The net monetary value of this placement after deducting agency commission from the gross contracted value. Represents the actual cost remitted to the media vendor. Part of the MONETARY_TRIPLET net total.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.placement_code IS 'External business identifier or SKU for the placement position, used in media planning and buying systems.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.placement_name IS 'Human-readable name describing the placement position (e.g., Homepage Leaderboard, In-Stream Pre-Roll, Sidebar Rectangle, Sponsored Post Slot).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.placement_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the placement position in inventory management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.placement_type IS 'Classification of the placement format type according to IAB standards. Code set: ref.placement_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.position IS 'The specific position or placement location within the site, broadcast, or publication (e.g., above-the-fold, pre-roll, homepage takeover, run-of-site). Directly impacts CPM rate, viewability, and audience engagement. Code set: ref.position.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.position_type IS 'Specific position classification within the property page or content stream, critical for viewability and engagement benchmarks. Code set: ref.position_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.rate_type IS 'The pricing model applied to this placement: Cost Per Mille (CPM), Cost Per Click (CPC), Cost Per Acquisition (CPA), Cost Per View (CPV), flat fee, Gross Rating Point (GRP), or Target Rating Point (TRP). Determines how contracted units are measured and billed. Code set: ref.rate_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.site_name IS 'The name of the specific website, TV station, radio station, publication, or network where the ad will run (e.g., ''CNN.com'', ''NBC Nightly News'', ''The New York Times''). Represents the RESOURCE_REFERENCE for the media property being purchased.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.targeting_parameters IS 'Descriptive summary of the audience and contextual targeting criteria applied to this placement (e.g., ''Adults 25-54, HHI $75K+, Interest: Auto, Geo: US-NY''). Captures demographic, geographic, behavioral, and contextual targeting as configured in The Trade Desk or Google CM360. Free-text summary for operational reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.third_party_verification_required IS 'Flag indicating whether third-party verification tags (viewability, brand safety, fraud detection) are required for this placement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.trafficking_notes IS 'Free-text operational notes entered by the ad operations team during trafficking in Google Campaign Manager 360, including special instructions, creative rotation rules, technical requirements, or vendor-specific delivery notes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.trafficking_status IS 'Current operational status of the placement in the ad trafficking workflow. Tracks the placement lifecycle from initial setup through live delivery to completion. Code set: ref.trafficking_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.vast_tag_required IS 'Flag indicating whether this placement requires VAST tag implementation for video ad serving.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.viewability_rate_benchmark_pct IS 'Historical or guaranteed viewability rate benchmark for this placement, measured per Media Rating Council (MRC) standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.viewability_target_pct IS 'The minimum viewability percentage contracted or targeted for this digital placement, per MRC viewability standards (e.g., 70% viewable impressions). Used to set vendor accountability thresholds and trigger make-good provisions in the IO.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.vpaid_supported IS 'Flag indicating whether this placement supports VPAID interactive video ad units.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_placement.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.plan IS 'Master record representing a structured media plan developed during the media planning phase. Captures plan name, client, campaign reference, planning period, total planned budget, target audience, channel mix allocation, GRP/TRP delivery targets, reach and frequency objectives, target markets/DMAs, demographic targets, approval status, and planner ownership. Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma. Serves as the SSOT for planned media strategy before buying execution begins.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.plan_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the media plan record in the Databricks Silver Layer. Primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser/client for whom this media plan is developed. Aligns with the Salesforce CRM account record. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: A media plan is executed under a specific agency-client AOR relationship, which governs commission rates, scope of services, and approval workflows applied to the plan. Planners must reference the AOR LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.agency_relationship.agency_relationship_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Media plans are developed at the brand level — brand guidelines, safety requirements, SOV targets, and budget allocations are brand-specific. Brand-level media planning is a core advertising workflow; LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign this media plan supports. Links the media plan to its overarching campaign strategy and objectives.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Media plans must be assigned to cost centers for budget planning, approval workflows, and financial accountability in campaign planning processes. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.creative_brief_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_brief. Business justification: Media plans are built from creative briefs that define messaging, audience, deliverables, and mandatories. Planners reference the brief throughout planning to ensure media strategy aligns with creativ LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.creative_brief.creative_brief_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: Media plans tied to specific budgets for planning, approval workflows, and budget allocation - fundamental financial planning relationship. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Media plans are budget authorization documents requiring GL account coding for revenue recognition and cost allocation reporting. Agency finance teams code plans to GL accounts to support P&L reportin LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Media plans are tracked as projects/initiatives in project management systems. Currently workfront_project_id is stored as an unlinked string. Normalizing to initiative_id FK enables joining to projec LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.persona_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.persona. Business justification: Persona-based media planning: media plans are strategically built around target personas (channel mix, daypart, content preferences). A domain expert expects the plan to reference the persona driving LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.persona.persona_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Media plans define primary target audience segments for campaign planning, budget allocation, and channel mix decisions. Core planning workflow requires linking plan to specific audience segment for t LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Media plans are executed under SOWs that authorize budget and scope. Planners reference the governing SOW for budget authority validation and scope compliance checks. Essential for financial controls LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.agency_commission_pct IS 'The percentage of the gross media budget retained by the agency as commission. Standard industry rate is typically 15%. Used in financial reconciliation and P&L reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.approval_date IS 'The date on which the media plan received formal client or internal approval. Marks the transition from planning to buying execution phase.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.approval_status IS 'The client or internal approval status of the media plan. Tracks whether the plan has been formally approved by the client before buying execution commences. Managed via Workfront approval workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the client contact or internal stakeholder who formally approved this media plan. Captured for audit trail and accountability purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.buying_approach IS 'The media buying methodology planned for this plan — direct IO-based buying, programmatic Real-Time Bidding (RTB) via DSP, or a hybrid approach. Determines execution path in Mediaocean Prisma and The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.channel_mix IS 'Comma-separated list of media channels included in this plan (e.g., ''digital_display, paid_social, ctv, ooh, broadcast_tv''). Defines the cross-channel strategy. Detailed channel-level budget splits are captured in child media plan line records.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code in which the media plan budget and financial targets are denominated (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.daypart_strategy IS 'The planned daypart scheduling strategy for broadcast and digital media placements. Defines when within the day media will be concentrated to maximize target audience reach.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.flight_end_date IS 'The date on which the planned media activity concludes in-market. Defines the end of the planning period. Nullable for open-ended or evergreen plans.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.flight_start_date IS 'The date on which the planned media activity begins running in-market. Defines the start of the planning period and aligns with insertion order (IO) effective dates in Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.frequency_target IS 'The planned average number of times a member of the target audience is exposed to the advertising during the flight period. Balances reach objectives against budget constraints.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.geographic_scope IS 'The geographic coverage level of the media plan, indicating whether the campaign runs nationally, regionally, locally, or internationally. Drives media buying strategy and publisher selection.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.grp_target IS 'The planned Gross Rating Point (GRP) delivery target for this media plan, representing the total weight of advertising exposure across the total population. Tracked via Nielsen Ad Intel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.is_addressable IS 'Indicates whether this media plan includes addressable media components (e.g., addressable TV, CTV/OTT targeting at household level). Triggers additional data governance and privacy compliance requirements under GDPR/CCPA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.is_programmatic IS 'Indicates whether this media plan includes programmatic buying components executed via a Demand-Side Platform (DSP) such as The Trade Desk. Drives workflow routing and technology fee accounting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.net_budget IS 'The net media budget after deducting agency commission and applicable fees from the gross planned budget. Represents the actual spend allocated to media vendors and publishers.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.plan_name IS 'Human-readable descriptive name of the media plan, typically including client name, campaign flight, and planning period (e.g., ''Acme Q3 2025 Brand Awareness Plan''). Used in Mediaocean Prisma and client presentations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.plan_number IS 'Externally-known unique business identifier for the media plan as assigned by Mediaocean Prisma. Used in client-facing documents, insertion orders, and cross-system references.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.plan_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the media plan within the planning and buying workflow. Drives downstream buying execution in Mediaocean Prisma. Code set: ref.plan_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.plan_type IS 'Classification of the media plan by strategic objective and buying approach. Determines the KPI framework and channel mix strategy applied. Code set: ref.plan_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.primary_kpi IS 'The primary Key Performance Indicator (KPI) against which this media plan''s success will be measured. Drives optimization strategy and reporting framework. Code set: ref.primary_kpi.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.prisma_plan_code IS 'The native plan identifier assigned by Mediaocean Prisma, the system of record for media planning and buying. Used for cross-system reconciliation between the lakehouse and Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.reach_target_pct IS 'The planned percentage of the target audience to be reached at least once during the flight period. A core media planning objective used to evaluate channel mix effectiveness.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.sfdc_opportunity_code IS 'The Salesforce CRM Opportunity ID associated with this media plan. Links the media plan to the sales pipeline record for revenue tracking and account management reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.target_age_range IS 'The primary demographic age range targeted by this media plan (e.g., ''25-54'', ''18-34''). Used for GRP/TRP calculation and audience buying parameters in Nielsen Ad Intel and The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.target_cpm IS 'The planned Cost Per Mille (CPM) — cost per 1,000 impressions — used as the benchmark rate for this media plan. Informs rate card negotiations and programmatic bid strategies in The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.target_gender IS 'Gender targeting parameter for the media plan audience. Informs GRP/TRP delivery targets and audience buying configurations in Nielsen Ad Intel and The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.target_markets IS 'Comma-separated list of target geographic markets or Designated Market Areas (DMAs) where media will run (e.g., ''New York DMA, Los Angeles DMA, Chicago DMA''). Used for geo-targeting and local market buying.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.total_planned_budget IS 'The gross total budget allocated to this media plan across all channels and placements for the full flight period. Expressed in the plan currency. Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma budget module.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.trp_target IS 'The planned Target Rating Point (TRP) delivery target for this media plan, representing the total weight of advertising exposure within the defined target audience demographic. Tracked via Nielsen Ad Intel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.version IS 'Version identifier of the media plan (e.g., v1.0, v2.3). Tracks iterative revisions submitted for client review or internal approval. Mediaocean Prisma supports versioned plan management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.plan_line IS 'Individual line-item within a media plan representing a specific channel, vehicle, and flight combination. Captures line number, media type (TV, digital, OOH, print, OTT/CTV, DOOH), vehicle name, market, start/end dates, planned units, planned GRPs/TRPs, planned impressions, planned CPM/CPC/CPA, planned spend, and approval status. Enables granular budget allocation and channel-level planning visibility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.plan_line_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for each individual line item within a media plan. Primary key for this entity. TRANSACTION_LINE role — each line represents one channel/vehicle/flight combination within a parent media plan.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: plan_line currently has media_type and media_subtype as STRING attributes. Each plan line represents a specific channel, vehicle, and flight combination. While plan_line → media_placement → ad_channel';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.ad_format_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_format. Business justification: plan_line currently has ad_format as a STRING attribute. Each plan line specifies the ad format for the planned media (e.g., 300x250 Banner, Pre-roll Video). This FK normalizes the plan_line-to-format';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.asset_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.asset. Business justification: Plan lines specify which creative assets will run in each placement. Essential for trafficking planning, publisher spec validation, and ensuring creative is ready before media flights begin. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign this media plan line supports. Links the line item to the overarching campaign strategy and objectives for cross-campaign reporting and budget tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: Media planners validate planned CPMs/rates against negotiated contract rate cards during plan line creation. This link enables rate compliance reporting — confirming planned spend aligns with contract LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Plan lines often allocated to specific cost centers for granular budget tracking and cross-functional cost allocation in matrix organizations. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.creative_brief_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_brief. Business justification: Plan lines are built to fulfill creative brief requirements (channel, format, audience). In multi-brand or multi-brief campaigns, individual plan lines may reference different briefs than the parent p LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.creative_brief.creative_brief_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Plan lines represent individual media cost commitments by channel/format. GL account coding at the line level enables granular cost classification for financial reporting, supporting channel-level P&L LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: A plan line is executed via a media insertion order — the IO is the contractual instrument that authorizes the buy for that plan line. Adding media_insertion_order_id to plan_line provides direct trac';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the specific media placement or ad unit associated with this line item. Links to the placement master record defining the ad environment, size, and position. RESOURCE_REFERENCE per TRANSACTION_LINE canonical role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.plan_id IS 'Reference to the parent media plan that contains this line item. Establishes the header/detail relationship between the media plan and its individual line items. HEADER_REFERENCE per TRANSACTION_LINE canonical role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Unique deal identifier for programmatic private marketplace (PMP) or programmatic guaranteed (PG) transactions associated with this line item. Used in The Trade Desk and DSP platforms for deal activation and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.publisher_id IS 'FK to vendor.publisher';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.publisher_property_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.publisher_property. Business justification: A plan line specifies the exact publisher property (vehicle) where the ad will run — e.g., CNN.com, ESPN App, NBC broadcast. plan_line currently has vehicle_name (STRING) which is a denormalized refer';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Plan lines specify granular audience targeting for individual media vehicles and tactics. Buyers need explicit segment linkage for rate negotiation, inventory availability checks, and delivery forecas LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.agency_commission_pct IS 'Percentage of gross media spend retained by the agency as commission for this line item. Standard advertising industry compensation model (historically 15%). Used for net spend calculation and client billing transparency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.approval_status IS 'Current workflow approval status of this media plan line item. Governs whether the line is authorized for buying and trafficking. LIFECYCLE_STATUS per TRANSACTION_LINE canonical role. Tracks progression from draft through client and internal approval gates.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.buying_status IS 'Operational buying and trafficking status of this line item, tracking progression from plan through insertion order issuance, confirmation, trafficking, and delivery. Distinct from approval_status which governs internal authorization. Code set: ref.buying_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.buying_type IS 'The pricing and buying model for this line item, determining how media is purchased and measured. CPM (Cost Per Mille), CPC (Cost Per Click), CPA (Cost Per Acquisition), CPV (Cost Per View), flat_rate, GRP (Gross Rating Point), or TRP (Target Rating Point). Drives rate card application and performance benchmarking. Code set: ref.buying_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.country_code IS 'ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code for the geographic territory where this media line item will be delivered (e.g., USA, GBR, CAN). Required for international campaign management and regulatory compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for all monetary values on this line item (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Required for multi-currency campaign management and financial consolidation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.daypart IS 'Broadcast or digital daypart specification for this line item, defining the time-of-day window for ad delivery (e.g., primetime, daytime, late_night). Critical for broadcast TV/radio buying and audience composition planning. Code set: ref.daypart.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.flight_end_date IS 'The date on which ad delivery for this media plan line item is scheduled to end. Defines the close of the flight period. Used for pacing, reconciliation, and campaign wrap-up reporting. EFFECTIVE_UNTIL per TRANSACTION_LINE canonical role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.flight_start_date IS 'The date on which ad delivery for this media plan line item is scheduled to begin. Defines the start of the flight period for trafficking, scheduling, and pacing purposes. EFFECTIVE_FROM per TRANSACTION_LINE canonical role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.is_bonus IS 'Indicates whether this line item represents bonus or added-value inventory provided by the publisher at no additional cost as part of a negotiated package. Bonus lines are excluded from spend calculations but included in delivery and GRP reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.is_makegood IS 'Indicates whether this line item is a makegood — compensatory inventory provided by the publisher to replace underdelivered or preempted spots from a prior buy. Makegood lines require special reconciliation treatment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.line_name IS 'Descriptive name for this media plan line item, typically combining the vehicle, placement, and flight period (e.g., ''CNN Homepage Takeover - Q1 2025''). Used for human-readable identification in reports and insertion orders.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.line_number IS 'Sequential line number identifying the position of this line item within the parent media plan. Used for ordering, referencing, and reconciliation against insertion orders and vendor invoices. LINE_SEQUENCE per TRANSACTION_LINE canonical role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.market IS 'Geographic market or designated market area (DMA) where this media line item will run (e.g., ''New York DMA'', ''National'', ''Los Angeles DMA''). Critical for audience targeting, GRP/TRP calculation, and local vs. national budget allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.media_subtype IS 'Granular classification within the media type (e.g., display, video, paid_search, social, connected_tv, digital_out_of_home, programmatic, direct). Enables detailed channel-level performance analysis and buying strategy differentiation. Code set: ref.media_subtype.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.media_type IS 'High-level classification of the media channel for this line item (e.g., digital, television, radio, print, out_of_home, cinema). Drives planning methodology, buying approach, and metric selection. Code set: ref.media_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_cpa IS 'Planned Cost Per Acquisition (CPA) — the negotiated or estimated cost for each conversion or acquisition event generated by this line item. Used for performance-based buying where payment is tied to measurable outcomes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_cpc IS 'Planned Cost Per Click (CPC) — the negotiated or estimated cost for each click generated by this line item. Primary pricing metric for paid search and performance-based digital campaigns. Applicable when buying_type is CPC.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_cpm IS 'Planned Cost Per Mille (CPM) — the negotiated or estimated cost per 1,000 impressions for this line item. Core pricing metric for digital and broadcast media buying. Used for rate benchmarking, budget allocation, and vendor negotiation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_frequency IS 'Planned average number of times a member of the target audience will be exposed to the ad during the flight period. Used with reach to calculate GRPs and to optimize against frequency caps and diminishing returns thresholds.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_grps IS 'Planned Gross Rating Points (GRPs) for this line item, representing total audience delivery as a percentage of the total target population. Primary planning metric for broadcast TV, radio, and OOH. Calculated as reach × frequency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_impressions IS 'The total number of ad impressions planned for this line item across the flight period. Standardized cross-channel metric used for reach estimation, CPM calculation, and campaign delivery forecasting regardless of buying type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_net_spend IS 'Planned net media spend after agency commission, discounts, and negotiated rebates have been deducted from the gross planned spend. Used for vendor payment reconciliation and agency P&L reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_reach_pct IS 'Planned percentage of the target audience expected to be exposed to the ad at least once during the flight period. Key media planning metric used alongside frequency to evaluate campaign effectiveness and GRP decomposition.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_spend IS 'Total planned gross media spend allocated to this line item for the full flight period, in the plan currency. Primary budget field used for financial planning, client billing, and P&L management. LINE_VALUE_OR_RESULT per TRANSACTION_LINE canonical role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_trps IS 'Planned Target Rating Points (TRPs) for this line item, representing audience delivery specifically among the defined target demographic as a percentage of that target population. More precise than GRPs for audience-specific campaign planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.planned_units IS 'The planned quantity of media units to be purchased for this line item. Unit interpretation depends on buying_type: impressions for CPM, clicks for CPC, conversions for CPA, spots for broadcast, panels for OOH. LINE_QUANTITY per TRANSACTION_LINE canonical role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.plan_line.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.schedule IS 'Operational master record representing the detailed airing/delivery schedule for purchased media placements — specifying exactly when and where ads will run across all channels. Captures schedule name, channel/vehicle, market/DMA, scheduled air dates and times, daypart classification (early morning, daytime, prime, late night, overnight, weekend), ad unit/format, creative rotation instructions, pod position (for broadcast), scheduled impressions/units per period, frequency cap, trafficking status, and last-updated timestamp. Daypart classification follows Nielsen standard daypart definitions. Sourced from Google Campaign Manager 360 trafficking and Mediaocean Prisma scheduling modules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.schedule_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the media schedule record. Primary key for the media_schedule data product in the Databricks Silver Layer.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: schedule currently has channel_type as a STRING attribute. schedule is the detailed airing/delivery schedule for purchased media placements. Each schedule is for a specific advertising channel. While';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.ad_format_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_format. Business justification: schedule currently has ad_unit_format as a STRING attribute. Each schedule specifies the ad format for delivery (e.g., 30-second TV spot, 300x250 Banner). This FK normalizes the schedule-to-format rel';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.asset_id IS 'Reference to the primary creative asset assigned to this media schedule slot. For rotation schedules, this represents the default or primary creative. Links to the creative master record. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.buy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.buy. Business justification: A schedule is the detailed airing/delivery schedule for a purchased media buy. The buy is the transactional commitment (the business event of purchasing media), and the schedule details WHEN and HOW t';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent advertising campaign under which this media schedule is executed. Enables campaign-level roll-up of all scheduled media activity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Scheduled media requires cost center for accrual posting and expense recognition timing in financial close processes. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Broadcast schedules represent committed airtime costs requiring GL account coding for accrual accounting. TV/radio schedule entries drive media cost accruals; GL coding at schedule level is standard i LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Schedules execute initiative-level media strategies. Linking enables initiative performance dashboards, strategic flight pattern analysis, and cross-campaign reach/frequency optimization required for LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Reference to the Insertion Order (IO) that authorises the purchase of this scheduled media. The IO is the contractual document between the advertiser/agency and the media vendor.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the media placement this schedule governs — the specific ad unit slot purchased on a publisher property. Links to the placement master record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.plan_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan_line. Business justification: A schedule entry represents the detailed airing/delivery execution of a specific plan line. Adding plan_line_id to schedule provides direct traceability from the operational delivery schedule back to';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Unique deal identifier for programmatic guaranteed or private marketplace (PMP) transactions, as assigned by the Supply-Side Platform (SSP) or publisher. Used to activate and reconcile programmatic deals in The Trade Desk DSP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Schedules define when and where ads run against specific audience segments for daypart and vehicle optimization. Planners use segment linkage for reach/frequency modeling and flighting strategy by aud LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Schedules represent execution of media buys authorized under a SOW. Linking schedule to sow enables SOW delivery tracking — confirming scheduled impressions/units are within contractually authorized s LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Schedule records represent actual media delivery execution by a specific supplier (TV station, radio network, digital vendor). Linking schedule to supplier enables vendor delivery performance reportin';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.trafficking_instruction_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.trafficking_instruction. Business justification: A schedule entry represents a specific airing/delivery slot that is governed by trafficking instructions sent to the ad server. One trafficking instruction can cover multiple schedule entries (e.g., m';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.vendor_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.vendor_rate_card. Business justification: Schedule lines carry cpm_rate and net_cost. Rate card compliance audits require tracing each scheduled rate back to the contracted vendor_rate_card. This is a standard media billing reconciliation pro';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.ad_duration_seconds IS 'Length of the ad creative in seconds, applicable to broadcast TV, radio, CTV/OTT, and digital video formats (e.g., 15, 30, 60). Used for broadcast trafficking, pod position management, and VAST/VPAID configuration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.air_end_time IS 'Precise date-time at which the ad unit is scheduled to stop airing or delivering on a given occurrence. Used alongside air_start_time to define the exact delivery window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.air_start_time IS 'Precise date-time at which the ad unit is scheduled to begin airing or delivering on a given occurrence. Critical for broadcast trafficking and programmatic deal scheduling. Stored in ISO 8601 format with timezone offset.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.buying_type IS 'Method by which the media inventory was purchased — direct IO, programmatic guaranteed, private marketplace (PMP) deal, open exchange, or Real-Time Bidding (RTB). Determines trafficking path and reconciliation process.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.cpm_rate IS 'Negotiated Cost Per Mille (CPM) — the cost per 1,000 ad impressions for this scheduled placement. Primary pricing metric for digital and programmatic media. Used for rate card benchmarking and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.creative_rotation_type IS 'Instruction governing how multiple creative assets are rotated across scheduled impressions — even (equal distribution), weighted (percentage-based), sequential (ordered), or optimised (performance-driven). Trafficked into Google Campaign Manager 360.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the net and gross cost amounts on this media schedule (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Enables multi-currency media buying and financial consolidation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.daypart IS 'Nielsen standard daypart classification indicating the time-of-day segment in which the ad is scheduled to air. Drives audience composition, CPM pricing, and GRP/TRP calculations. Values follow Nielsen daypart definitions. Code set: ref.daypart.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.dma_code IS 'Nielsen-assigned three-digit numeric code identifying the Designated Market Area (DMA) for broadcast and local media scheduling. Enables standardised geographic audience measurement and GRP/TRP reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.flight_end_date IS 'The last calendar date on which ads are scheduled to air or deliver under this media schedule. Defines the closing boundary of the campaign flight period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.flight_start_date IS 'The first calendar date on which ads are scheduled to air or deliver under this media schedule. Defines the opening boundary of the campaign flight period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.frequency_cap IS 'Maximum number of times a unique user or household may be served this ad within the defined frequency cap period. Controls ad fatigue and audience experience. Trafficked into Google Campaign Manager 360 and The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.frequency_cap_period IS 'Time window over which the frequency cap applies — hour, day, week, month, or lifetime of the campaign. Works in conjunction with frequency_cap to define the full frequency capping rule.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.gross_cost IS 'Gross cost of the scheduled media buy before agency commission deduction, expressed in the billing currency. Represents the full rate card value billed by the media vendor.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.is_makegood IS 'Flag indicating whether this schedule record represents a make-good — a compensatory placement provided by the media vendor to offset an under-delivery or missed airing from a prior schedule. Critical for reconciliation and vendor performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.market_name IS 'Geographic market or Designated Market Area (DMA) where the media will air or be delivered — e.g., ''New York'', ''Los Angeles'', ''National''. Used for local vs. national media planning and GRP/TRP calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.net_cost IS 'Net cost of the scheduled media buy after agency commission and negotiated discounts, expressed in the billing currency. Used for budget management, P&L reporting, and financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.pod_position IS 'Requested or guaranteed position of the ad within a commercial break pod for broadcast TV, radio, and CTV/OTT channels. First and last pod positions command premium pricing. Null for non-broadcast channels.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.preemptible IS 'Flag indicating whether this scheduled placement can be preempted by a higher-paying advertiser. Preemptible spots are typically priced lower than guaranteed placements. Relevant for broadcast and premium digital inventory.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.schedule_name IS 'Human-readable name assigned to this media schedule record, typically reflecting the campaign flight, channel, and market (e.g., ''Q3_BrandLaunch_PrimeTV_NYC''). Used for trafficking and reporting identification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.schedule_number IS 'Externally-known alphanumeric reference number for this schedule, as assigned by the media planning system (Mediaocean Prisma) or trafficking system (Google Campaign Manager 360). Used for cross-system reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.scheduled_grp IS 'Total Gross Rating Points (GRP) planned for this media schedule, representing the sum of ratings across all scheduled airings. GRP = Reach % × Frequency. Used for broadcast media planning and audience delivery measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.scheduled_impressions IS 'Total number of ad impressions contracted and scheduled for delivery under this media schedule record for the defined flight period. Used for pacing, delivery tracking, and reconciliation against actuals.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.scheduled_trp IS 'Total Target Rating Points (TRP) planned for this media schedule, measuring GRP delivery against a specific target audience demographic. TRP is the audience-qualified subset of GRP used for precision media planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.scheduled_units IS 'Number of discrete ad units (spots, insertions, or placements) scheduled for the flight period — applicable to broadcast (spots), print (insertions), and OOH (faces/panels). Distinct from impressions which measure audience exposure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.source_system_ref IS 'Native record identifier from the originating operational system — Google Campaign Manager 360 placement ID or Mediaocean Prisma schedule line number. Enables traceability and reconciliation back to the system of record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.trafficking_notes IS 'Free-text field for trafficking instructions, special placement requirements, or operational notes associated with this media schedule — e.g., ''Run adjacent to news content only'', ''Avoid competitor adjacency''. Sourced from Google Campaign Manager 360 trafficking comments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.trafficking_status IS 'Current operational status of this media schedule in the trafficking workflow. Tracks progression from initial planning through creative assignment, trafficking into ad server, live delivery, and completion or cancellation. Sourced from Google Campaign Manager 360. Code set: ref.trafficking_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.vehicle_name IS 'Name of the specific media vehicle (publisher, network, station, or platform) where the ad will be delivered — e.g., ''NBC Primetime'', ''New York Times Digital'', ''Spotify'', ''Clear Channel OOH''. Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma publisher library.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.schedule.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.buy IS 'Transactional record capturing the execution of a media purchase — the business event of committing agency/client spend to a specific media vehicle against an authorized IO and plan line. Captures buy date, buyer name, vendor, channel, buy type (upfront, scatter, programmatic RTB, direct, retail media network, CTV/OTT addressable), buy status (pending, confirmed, cancelled), negotiated rate, total buy value, authorized spend ceiling, DSP/SSP reference (The Trade Desk deal ID for programmatic), market type (upfront commitment/scatter opportunistic/makeweight), upfront deal year reference for broadcast, and reconciliation status. Supports all buying modalities including traditional broadcast (linear, addressable), digital direct, programmatic (display, video, CTV, audio), and emerging retail media network purchases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.buy_id IS 'Unique system-generated identifier for the media buy record. Primary key for this transactional entity. TRANSACTION_HEADER role — represents the discrete business event of committing agency/client spend to a specific media vehicle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: buy currently has channel as a STRING attribute. buy is the transactional purchase event, and each buy is for a specific advertising channel (e.g., Display, Video, Search). While buy → media_placement';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.ad_format_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_format. Business justification: buy currently has format as a STRING attribute. Each buy is for a specific ad format (e.g., 300x250 Banner, Pre-roll Video). This FK normalizes the buy-to-format relationship, replacing the string att';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.asset_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.asset. Business justification: Buyers need to know which creative asset will run in each buy for trafficking instructions, publisher spec validation, and delivery verification. Critical for makegood and reconciliation processes. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: Media buyers must confirm negotiated buy rates conform to the contracted rate card — a core billing audit and reconciliation process. Linking buy to contract_rate_card enables rate variance reporting LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Media buys require cost center for expense tracking, financial reconciliation, and variance reporting - core financial control requirement. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: Media buys must reference budgets for spend tracking, variance analysis, and budget compliance monitoring in financial management. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Media buys are the transactional unit generating vendor payables. GL account coding at the buy level is required for accounts payable posting and cost accrual. Agency finance systems require buy-to-GL LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Media buys roll up to initiatives for consolidated financial tracking. Required for initiative-level ROI analysis, strategic performance measurement, and cross-campaign budget reconciliation in agency LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Reference to the authorizing Insertion Order (IO) under which this media buy is executed. Links the buy to its contractual authorization and spend ceiling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the specific media placement or ad unit being purchased (e.g., a specific ad slot, daypart, or digital placement). Links to the placement master in the media domain.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.plan_line_id IS 'Reference to the specific media plan line item this buy executes against. Ties the transactional buy back to the approved media plan for reconciliation and pacing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.programmatic_deal. Business justification: buy is the transactional record of a media purchase. While buy → plan_line → programmatic_deal path exists, many buys are directly associated with a specific programmatic deal (PMP, programmatic guara';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Media buys execute against defined audience targets for delivery and measurement. Buyers negotiate rates and inventory based on specific segment reach and composition. Essential for buy reconciliation LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Media buys are authorized under a specific SOW that defines the contractual scope and budget. Linking buy to sow enables SOW budget consumption tracking and ensures each buy is executed within the cor LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the media vendor or publisher from whom the media inventory is purchased (e.g., broadcast network, digital publisher, OOH operator). Maps to the vendor master.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.added_value_flag IS 'Indicates whether this buy includes added-value inventory (bonus impressions, sponsored content, or value-add placements) negotiated as part of the overall media deal at no incremental cost to the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.agency_commission_amount IS 'Agency commission deducted from the gross buy amount, typically 15% of gross per industry standard. Represents the agency''s compensation component embedded in the media buy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.authorized_spend_ceiling IS 'Maximum spend amount authorized for this media buy as approved on the Insertion Order or client budget authorization. Acts as a financial control limit; actual spend must not exceed this value.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.booked_units IS 'Quantity of media delivery units contracted in this buy (e.g., number of impressions, GRPs, TRPs, clicks, or spots). The unit type is defined by the rate_basis field. Used for pacing and delivery reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.buy_date IS 'The principal real-world business event date on which the media buy was executed — i.e., the date the agency committed spend to the media vehicle. Distinct from system audit timestamps.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.buy_number IS 'Externally-known alphanumeric identifier for the media buy, used in communications with vendors, on Insertion Orders, and in billing reconciliation. Corresponds to the buy reference number in Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.buy_status IS 'Current workflow lifecycle state of the media buy. Drives operational actions: pending = awaiting vendor confirmation; confirmed = vendor-accepted and active; cancelled = buy voided; paused = temporarily halted; completed = delivery fulfilled.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.buy_type IS 'Classification of the buying modality used to acquire this media inventory. Upfront = advance commitment; scatter = opportunistic spot market; programmatic RTB = real-time bidding via DSP; direct = direct IO with publisher; retail media = retail media network purchase; CTV addressable = addressable CTV/OTT buy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.cancellation_date IS 'Date on which this media buy was cancelled, if applicable. Populated only when buy_status = ''cancelled''. Used for cancellation liability calculations and vendor notification tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.cancellation_reason IS 'Reason code for the cancellation of this media buy. Required when buy_status = ''cancelled'' to support financial liability assessment and vendor relationship management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code in which the buy amounts are denominated (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Required for multi-currency campaign management and financial consolidation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.delivery_status IS 'Current state of media inventory delivery against the booked buy. Tracks whether the vendor has fulfilled the contracted impressions, GRPs, or other delivery units. Underdelivery triggers makegoods; overdelivery may require credit memos.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.flight_end_date IS 'The date on which media delivery for this buy is scheduled to conclude. Defines the end of the active delivery window. Used for pacing, reconciliation, and billing cutoff.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.flight_start_date IS 'The date on which media delivery for this buy is scheduled to begin. Defines the start of the active delivery window (flight period) for trafficking and scheduling purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.gross_buy_amount IS 'Total gross value of the media buy before agency commission, discounts, or adjustments. Represents the full billing value to the vendor as stated on the Insertion Order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.makegood_flag IS 'Indicates whether this media buy is a makegood — compensatory inventory provided by the vendor to remedy underdelivery or audience guarantee shortfalls on a prior buy. True = this is a makegood buy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.market_type IS 'Broadcast market commitment classification. Upfront = advance season commitment at negotiated rates; scatter = opportunistic in-season purchase at prevailing market rates; makeweight = inventory added to fulfill audience delivery guarantees (GRP/TRP shortfall).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.negotiated_rate IS 'The unit rate negotiated with the vendor for this media buy, expressed in the applicable rate basis (e.g., CPM, CPC, CPA, GRP cost). This is the commercially sensitive contracted rate, distinct from rate card pricing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.net_buy_amount IS 'Net cost of the media buy after deducting agency commission from the gross amount. Represents the actual vendor payment obligation. Net = Gross minus Agency Commission.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.notes IS 'Free-text field for buyer annotations, special deal terms, negotiation notes, or operational instructions associated with this media buy. Not used for structured data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.prisma_buy_code IS 'Source system identifier for this buy record in Mediaocean Prisma, the system of record for media planning, buying, and billing. Used for system-of-record traceability and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.rate_basis IS 'The pricing metric on which the negotiated rate is denominated. CPM = Cost Per Mille (thousand impressions); CPC = Cost Per Click; CPA = Cost Per Acquisition; GRP = Gross Rating Point cost; flat = fixed fee; CPCV = Cost Per Completed View; vCPM = viewable CPM. Code set: ref.rate_basis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.reconciliation_status IS 'Current state of the financial reconciliation process for this media buy. Tracks whether vendor invoices have been matched against booked buy amounts. Unreconciled = not yet matched; in_progress = reconciliation underway; reconciled = fully matched; disputed = discrepancy under review; written_off = irreconcilable variance closed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.upfront_deal_year IS 'Broadcast season year reference for upfront market commitments (e.g., ''2024-2025''). Identifies the upfront buying cycle to which this buy belongs, enabling season-level budget tracking and audience guarantee management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.buy.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.media_insertion_order IS 'Authoritative master record for all Insertion Orders (IOs) issued to media vendors and publishers. Captures IO number, advertiser, agency, vendor, flight dates, total authorized spend, payment terms, cancellation policy, IO status (draft, executed, cancelled), and client authorization details (authorizing party, authorization date, authorization method). Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma and serves as the contractual backbone for all media buys. Links to media plans, placements, and vendor records.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the Insertion Order record. Primary key. Entity role: TRANSACTION_HEADER — this is a discrete contractual business event with a clear lifecycle (draft → executed → cancelled), carrying authorized spend, flight dates, and vendor/advertiser party references.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: media_insertion_order currently has channel_type as a STRING attribute. IOs are issued to media vendors for specific advertising channels (e.g., IO for Display advertising, IO for CTV). This FK normal';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser (client brand) on whose behalf this IO is issued. Links to the client.advertiser master record. Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER PARTY_REFERENCE category. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: IOs are issued under a specific agency-client relationship that determines commission rates, billing terms, and notice periods applied on the IO. IO-level agency relationship tracking is standard in m LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.agency_relationship.agency_relationship_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the overarching master service agreement or framework contract under which this IO is issued. Supports contract hierarchy and legal compliance tracking. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.agreement.agreement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: IOs authorize spend for a specific brand. Brand-level IO tracking is required for brand budget reconciliation, brand safety enforcement, and publisher-facing brand identification. Media buyers and fin LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign this IO supports. Enables campaign-level spend aggregation, KPI tracking, and ROAS reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Insertion orders require cost center assignment for budget allocation, financial reporting, and expense tracking - fundamental financial control in advertising operations. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: Insertion orders must reference approved budgets for spend authorization, compliance checking, and budget consumption tracking in financial controls. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: IOs are the primary financial commitment document in agency media operations. GL account coding at the IO level is required for accounts payable posting, accrual accounting, and financial statement cl LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Insertion orders execute within strategic initiatives. Linking enables portfolio-level budget management, cross-campaign spend analysis, and strategic alignment reporting required for client business LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.plan_id IS 'Reference to the parent media plan from which this IO was generated. Enables traceability from strategic plan through execution to billing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.publisher_id IS 'Reference to the media vendor or publisher receiving this IO. Links to the vendor master record for payment, reconciliation, and compliance checks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.publisher_property_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.publisher_property. Business justification: media_insertion_order currently has FK to publisher (parent entity). Many IOs are property-specific (e.g., IO for NYTimes.com, IO for WSJ Print Edition). While media_insertion_order → publisher → publ';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: An IO is issued under a specific SOW that authorizes the media spend — more granular than the master agreement already linked. Agencies track IO spend against SOW budgets for client billing and scope LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the internal agency entity (buying unit) issuing this IO on behalf of the advertiser. Supports multi-agency holding company structures and commission calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.vendor_rate_card_id IS 'Reference to the vendor rate card governing the pricing of placements under this IO. Links to the media rate card product for CPM, CPC, CPA, and flat-fee rate validation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.agency_commission_amount IS 'Agency commission deducted from the gross authorized spend, typically calculated as a percentage of gross billings (standard 15% of gross or negotiated rate). Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER MONETARY_TRIPLET (adjustment) category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.authorized_spend_amount IS 'Total gross media spend authorized under this IO, expressed in the IO currency. Represents the maximum contractual commitment to the vendor before agency commission and fees. Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER MONETARY_TRIPLET (gross base amount) category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.billing_cycle IS 'Frequency at which the vendor invoices against this IO. Drives accounts payable scheduling and cash flow forecasting in SAP S/4HANA FI.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.brand_safety_requirements IS 'Free-text or structured description of brand safety and suitability requirements contractually mandated for this IO (e.g., IAB content category exclusions, GARM brand safety floor). Enforced during trafficking and programmatic bid configuration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.buying_method IS 'The transactional mechanism used to purchase media under this IO. Distinguishes direct buys from Real-Time Bidding (RTB), programmatic guaranteed, and Private Marketplace (PMP) deals. Informs DSP/SSP configuration in The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.cancellation_notice_days IS 'Number of business days advance notice required to cancel this IO without incurring the full cancellation penalty. Operationalizes the cancellation policy for workflow and legal compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.cancellation_policy IS 'Contractual cancellation terms governing the IO. Specifies whether the IO can be cancelled, the required notice period, and any financial penalties. Critical for financial liability management and vendor negotiations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for all monetary amounts on this IO (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER MONETARY_TRIPLET (currency code) category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.execution_date IS 'The date on which the IO was formally executed (signed/authorized) by all parties. Represents the principal real-world business event timestamp at day granularity. Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER BUSINESS_EVENT_TIMESTAMP category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.flight_end_date IS 'The last date on which media placements under this IO are authorized to run. Defines the end of the contracted delivery window. Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER EFFECTIVE_UNTIL category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.flight_start_date IS 'The first date on which media placements under this IO are authorized to run. Defines the beginning of the contracted delivery window. Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER EFFECTIVE_FROM category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.guaranteed_impressions IS 'Total number of ad impressions contractually guaranteed by the vendor under this IO. Applicable for CPM and guaranteed programmatic buys. Used for delivery pacing and reconciliation against actuals.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.io_name IS 'Human-readable descriptive name for the IO, typically combining advertiser, campaign, channel, and flight period (e.g., ''BrandX_Q3_2024_Display_IO''). Used in Mediaocean Prisma and trafficking systems for quick identification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.io_number IS 'Externally-known, human-readable Insertion Order number assigned by Mediaocean Prisma at IO creation. Used on all vendor invoices, trafficking instructions, and reconciliation documents. Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER BUSINESS_IDENTIFIER category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.io_status IS 'Current workflow state of the Insertion Order. Drives downstream trafficking, billing, and reconciliation eligibility. Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER LIFECYCLE_STATUS category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.io_type IS 'Classification of the IO by buying method. Distinguishes direct buys from programmatic guaranteed, preferred deals, and private marketplace (PMP) deals. Informs DSP/SSP routing and billing treatment. Code set: ref.io_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.is_programmatic IS 'Indicates whether this IO governs programmatic media buying (True) or a direct/traditional buy (False). Used to route IO data to DSP/SSP systems such as The Trade Desk and to apply appropriate measurement and brand safety standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.makegood_policy IS 'Contractual make-good policy specifying how the vendor compensates for under-delivery against guaranteed impressions or GRPs. Options include credit against future buys, re-run of spots, or cash refund.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.net_spend_amount IS 'Net media cost payable to the vendor after deducting agency commission from the gross authorized spend. Used for vendor payment and reconciliation. Satisfies TRANSACTION_HEADER MONETARY_TRIPLET (net total) category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional contractual terms, special instructions, or operational notes associated with this IO that are not captured in structured fields. Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma IO comments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.payment_terms IS 'Contractual payment terms agreed with the vendor, specifying the number of days after invoice date by which payment is due (e.g., Net 30, Net 45). Drives accounts payable scheduling in SAP S/4HANA FI-AP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.po_number IS 'Client-issued Purchase Order number associated with this IO. Required by many advertisers for invoice matching and financial controls in SAP S/4HANA MM. Links the IO to the client''s internal procurement system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.pricing_model IS 'The cost pricing model agreed with the vendor for this IO. Determines how media delivery is measured and billed: Cost Per Mille (CPM), Cost Per Click (CPC), Cost Per Acquisition (CPA), Cost Per Completed View (CPCV), flat fee, or Cost Per View (CPV).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.prisma_io_code IS 'Native system identifier for this IO in Mediaocean Prisma. Enables direct cross-reference and reconciliation between the lakehouse Silver layer and the source system of record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.version_number IS 'Sequential version number incremented each time the IO is formally amended (e.g., spend increase, flight date change). Enables change history tracking and audit compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'The client-side contractual IO (CRM) that this vendor-facing media IO executes. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.media_insertion_order.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.programmatic_deal IS 'Master record for programmatic media deals negotiated with DSPs, SSPs, exchanges, and retail media networks — including Private Marketplace (PMP) deals, Preferred Deals, Programmatic Guaranteed (PG) deals, and retailer-specific programmatic inventory (Amazon DSP, Walmart Connect, Instacart Ads). Captures deal ID (The Trade Desk deal ID, Amazon DSP deal ID), deal name, deal type (PMP, PG, open auction, retailer PMP), DSP platform, SSP/exchange/retailer, publisher, CPM floor price, deal start/end dates, impression commitment, targeting parameters (including shopper/purchase data for RMN), deal status, RTB bid strategy, and closed-loop measurement availability flag. Sourced from The Trade Desk, Amazon DSP, and other programmatic platforms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the programmatic deal record. Entity role: MASTER_AGREEMENT — governs a binding programmatic inventory commitment between the agency/advertiser and a DSP/SSP/exchange/retailer.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: programmatic_deal currently has channel as a STRING attribute. Programmatic deals are negotiated for specific advertising channels (e.g., Programmatic Display deal, CTV deal). This FK normalizes the d';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.ad_format_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_format. Business justification: programmatic_deal currently has ad_format as a STRING attribute. Programmatic deals specify the ad format for the deal inventory (e.g., 300x250 Banner, Pre-roll Video). This FK normalizes the deal-to-';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser (client brand) on whose behalf this programmatic deal is negotiated and executed. Used for client-level reporting, billing, and competitive conflict checks. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.agreement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.agreement. Business justification: Programmatic deals (PMPs, preferred deals, guaranteed deals) are negotiated under a master agreement with the publisher. This link enables contract compliance tracking for programmatic inventory commi LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.agreement.agreement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Programmatic deals (PMPs, preferred deals) are negotiated at the brand level — brand safety tiers, audience targeting, and floor CPMs are brand-specific. Brand-level deal tracking is essential for com LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent advertising campaign under which this programmatic deal is executed. Links the deal to campaign-level objectives, KPIs, and budget in Google Campaign Manager 360 and The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Programmatic deals are cost-center-specific financial commitments in agency operations. Cost center attribution at the deal level is required for P&L reporting by business unit and client, and for int LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.dsp_tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Programmatic deals reference dsp_platform as plain text. Linking to tech_partner via dsp_tech_partner_id normalizes DSP vendor attribution, enabling programmatic tech fee tracking, DSP SLA management,';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: Programmatic deals carry a budget_amount commitment that must be tracked against an approved finance budget for spend control. Deal-level budget authorization is required for programmatic trading desk LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Programmatic deals are financial commitments with budget amounts requiring GL account coding for accrual accounting and cost classification. Deal-level GL coding supports programmatic spend reporting LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: programmatic_deal currently has io_number (STRING) which is a denormalized reference to the parent insertion order. Programmatic deals are executed under a master IO — the IO provides the contractual';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.publisher_id IS 'Unique identifier for the publisher as assigned by the SSP, exchange, or DSP platform. Used for supply path optimization, publisher-level reconciliation, and cross-platform publisher deduplication.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.publisher_property_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.publisher_property. Business justification: programmatic_deal currently has FK to publisher (parent entity). Many programmatic deals are property-specific (e.g., deal for NYTimes.com homepage, deal for WSJ Mobile App). While programmatic_deal →';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Programmatic deals (PMP/PG) are negotiated for specific audience segments with publishers and SSPs. Deal setup, activation, and performance measurement require explicit segment linkage for targeting c LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Programmatic deal setup requires matching the deal''s accepted creative formats (VAST version, ad unit size, viewability thresholds) to a creative spec. Ad ops teams perform spec-to-deal alignment duri LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.spec.spec_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.brand_safety_tier IS 'Brand safety classification applied to this deal, determining content adjacency restrictions and inventory quality controls. Configured per TAG (Trustworthy Accountability Group) Brand Safety standards and enforced via The Trade Desk and Google Campaign Manager 360.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.budget_amount IS 'Total monetary budget allocated to this programmatic deal in the deal currency. For PG deals, calculated as floor_cpm × impression_commitment / 1000. Used for financial planning, budget pacing, and P&L reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.closed_loop_measurement IS 'Indicates whether closed-loop measurement (linking ad exposure to purchase/conversion outcomes) is available for this deal. Particularly relevant for Retail Media Network (RMN) deals (Amazon DSP, Walmart Connect, Instacart Ads) where purchase data enables attribution. True = closed-loop measurement available.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for all monetary values on this deal (floor CPM, budget, etc.). Defaults to USD for most programmatic deals but supports multi-currency for international campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.deal_code IS 'Externally-known deal identifier assigned by the DSP or SSP/exchange (e.g., The Trade Desk deal ID, Amazon DSP deal ID). Used for trafficking, bid requests, and reconciliation across platforms. Maps to the deal_id field in The Trade Desk and OpenRTB bid-request objects.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.deal_name IS 'Human-readable name of the programmatic deal as entered in the DSP or Mediaocean Prisma. Used for identification in media plans, trafficking sheets, and reporting dashboards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.deal_source_system IS 'The operational system of record from which this programmatic deal record was sourced. Used for data lineage, reconciliation, and ETL pipeline routing. Drives system-specific field mapping ingestion process. Code set: ref.deal_source_system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.deal_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the programmatic deal. Draft = in negotiation; Pending Approval = submitted for internal/publisher approval; Active = live and eligible for bidding; Paused = temporarily suspended; Expired = past end date; Cancelled = terminated before end date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.deal_type IS 'Classification of the programmatic deal structure. PMP (Private Marketplace) = curated invite-only auction; Preferred Deal = fixed CPM, non-guaranteed; Programmatic Guaranteed (PG) = fixed CPM with impression commitment; Open Auction = RTB open exchange; Retailer PMP = retailer-specific private marketplace (e.g., Amazon DSP, Walmart Connect). Code set: ref.deal_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.end_date IS 'The date on which the programmatic deal expires and is no longer eligible for bidding. Nullable for evergreen deals with no fixed end. Used for pacing, reconciliation, and deal renewal workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.environment_type IS 'The technical environment in which the ad inventory is served (web browser, mobile app, CTV device, DOOH screen, audio stream). Determines applicable measurement standards, viewability metrics, and brand safety controls.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.external_deal_ref IS 'Secondary external reference identifier for this deal as recorded in a partner system (e.g., publisher deal ID, SSP deal reference, Mediaocean Prisma order number). Enables cross-system reconciliation and deduplication.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.floor_cpm IS 'The minimum Cost Per Mille (CPM) bid price in USD required to win impressions under this deal. For PMP and Preferred Deals, this is the negotiated floor; for PG deals, this is the fixed CPM. Critical for bid strategy configuration in The Trade Desk and financial forecasting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.frequency_cap IS 'Maximum number of times a unique user/device may be served an ad under this deal within the frequency cap period. Configured in The Trade Desk to control ad fatigue and optimize audience reach. Null indicates no frequency cap applied.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.frequency_cap_period IS 'The time window over which the frequency cap applies (hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, or lifetime of the deal). Used in conjunction with frequency_cap to configure audience exposure limits in The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.geo_targeting IS 'Geographic targeting scope for this deal, expressed as country codes, DMA regions, or postal codes (e.g., ''USA'', ''USA:DMA:501'', ''GBR''). Drives geo-based audience segmentation and regulatory compliance (GDPR for EU inventory, CCPA for California).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.impression_commitment IS 'The total number of impressions committed under this deal. Mandatory for Programmatic Guaranteed (PG) deals where delivery is contractually obligated. For PMP and Preferred Deals, represents the estimated or target impression volume. Used for pacing, delivery forecasting, and make-good calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.negotiated_timestamp IS 'The real-world business event timestamp when the programmatic deal was formally agreed/struck between the buyer and seller. Distinct from the record audit created timestamp. Used for deal velocity reporting and SLA tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.notes IS 'Free-text field for capturing deal-specific negotiation notes, special terms, publisher commitments, or operational instructions not captured in structured fields. Used by media buyers and account managers for deal context.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.rtb_bid_strategy IS 'The Real-Time Bidding (RTB) bid strategy configured in the DSP for this deal. Fixed CPM is standard for PG deals; Dynamic CPM and performance-based strategies (Target CPA, Target ROAS) apply to PMP and open auction deals. Configured in The Trade Desk Bid Management module.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.shopper_data_enabled IS 'Indicates whether retailer shopper/purchase data is used for audience targeting in this deal. Applicable to Retail Media Network (RMN) deals on Amazon DSP, Walmart Connect, and Instacart Ads. True = first-party shopper data targeting is active.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.start_date IS 'The date on which the programmatic deal becomes active and eligible for bidding. Corresponds to the deal flight start in The Trade Desk and Mediaocean Prisma. Used for media plan scheduling and budget pacing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.viewability_threshold_pct IS 'Minimum viewability rate (as a percentage) required for impressions under this deal to be counted as valid. Defined per MRC viewability standards (50% of pixels in view for 1 second for display; 50% for 2 seconds for video). Used for deal quality scoring and billing reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.programmatic_deal.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.trafficking_instruction IS 'Transactional record capturing ad trafficking instructions issued to ad servers and media vendors for creative asset delivery. Captures instruction type (new, revision, cancellation), placement reference, creative asset reference, ad server (Google Campaign Manager 360), VAST/VPAID tag URL, click-through URL, impression tracking pixels, viewability tags, brand safety parameters, trafficking date, trafficker name, and instruction status (pending, sent, confirmed). Represents the operational event of dispatching creative to media.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.trafficking_instruction_id IS 'Unique system-generated identifier for each ad trafficking instruction record issued to an ad server or media vendor. Serves as the primary key for this transactional entity. ROLE: TRANSACTION_HEADER.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: A trafficking instruction is channel-specific — different channels use different ad servers, tag formats (VAST vs. display tags), and trafficking protocols. Linking trafficking_instruction to ad_chann';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.ad_format_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_format. Business justification: trafficking_instruction currently has ad_format as a STRING attribute. Trafficking instructions specify the ad format for delivery to ad servers (e.g., 300x250 Banner, VAST 4.0 Video). This FK normali';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.asset_id IS 'Reference to the creative asset (banner, video, rich media, etc.) being dispatched via this trafficking instruction. Identifies the specific creative unit to be served at the designated placement. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.buy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.buy. Business justification: A trafficking instruction is issued to execute a specific media buy — it carries the creative assets, targeting parameters, and ad server tags needed to activate the purchased inventory. Linking traff';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent advertising campaign under which this trafficking instruction is issued. Provides campaign-level context for reporting and performance attribution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Trafficking instructions drive ad server costs (third-party verification, ad serving fees) that require cost center attribution. Agency operations allocate trafficking costs to cost centers for client LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.creative_brief_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_brief. Business justification: Trafficking teams must reference the creative brief to confirm spec compliance, messaging mandatories, and legal/regulatory requirements before sending ad tags. A trafficker needs to know which brief LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.creative_brief.creative_brief_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Reference to the Insertion Order (IO) authorizing the media buy associated with this trafficking instruction. Provides contractual and financial context for the ad delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the media placement for which this trafficking instruction is issued. Links the instruction to the specific ad unit, position, and publisher property where the creative will be delivered.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.parent_instruction_trafficking_instruction_id IS 'Reference to the original trafficking instruction that this record revises or cancels. Enables lineage tracking across instruction versions and supports audit of changes to creative delivery parameters.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.plan_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan_line. Business justification: Trafficking instructions are issued to execute specific media placements that originate from plan lines. Adding plan_line_id to trafficking_instruction provides direct traceability from the ad server';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.programmatic_deal. Business justification: Trafficking instructions for programmatic placements must reference the programmatic deal that governs the inventory access, floor CPM, targeting parameters, and DSP seat configuration. This FK enable';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Trafficking instructions configure ad server targeting parameters for specific audience segments. Ad ops teams require explicit segment linkage to set up DMP/DSP integrations, frequency caps, and audi LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Trafficking is a deliverable service often specified in SOWs with defined SLAs. Linking instructions to SOWs enables service-level tracking, supports billing for trafficking services, and validates sc LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Trafficking instructions specify exact creative spec requirements (ad size, VAST tag, file format) that must be validated before sending tags. The existing creative_size plain attribute is a denormali LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.spec.spec_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.suppression_list_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.suppression_list. Business justification: Privacy-compliant ad trafficking: trafficking instructions configure ad server delivery and must reference suppression lists (opted-out users, converted customers) to ensure GDPR/CCPA-compliant servin LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.suppression_list.suppression_list_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Trafficking instructions specify the ad server platform and brand safety/verification provider. Linking to tech_partner normalizes the ad_server plain-text field and enables vendor SLA tracking, tech';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.ad_server_placement_code IS 'The unique placement tag or code assigned by the ad server (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360 placement ID) that maps this instruction to the correct ad unit within the ad serving platform. Used for trafficking reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.brand_safety_provider IS 'Name of the third-party brand safety and suitability verification provider applied to this trafficking instruction. Ensures ad creative is served only in brand-appropriate content environments per TAG and GARM standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.brand_safety_segment IS 'Specific brand safety content category or segment classification applied to this instruction (e.g., ''exclude adult content'', ''exclude fake news'', ''GARM Floor''). Defines the content adjacency restrictions enforced during ad delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.click_through_url IS 'The destination URL to which users are redirected upon clicking the served ad creative. Must be validated and approved prior to trafficking. Critical for campaign performance tracking and landing page attribution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.confirmed_timestamp IS 'Precise date and time when the ad server or media vendor confirmed receipt and acceptance of the trafficking instruction. Used for SLA compliance measurement and operational reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.daypart_schedule IS 'Day-of-week and time-of-day scheduling parameters defining when the ad creative should be served (dayparting). Expressed as a structured schedule string (e.g., ''Mon-Fri 08:00-20:00''). Used to optimize delivery timing per media plan.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.delivery_end_date IS 'The scheduled date on which ad creative delivery is to cease per this trafficking instruction. Aligns with the media plan flight end dates and insertion order terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.delivery_start_date IS 'The scheduled date on which ad creative delivery is to commence per this trafficking instruction. Aligns with the media plan flight dates and insertion order terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.device_targeting IS 'Device type targeting parameters specifying which device categories the ad creative should be served on (e.g., desktop, mobile, tablet, Connected TV (CTV), or all devices). Aligns with media plan targeting specifications.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.frequency_cap_impressions IS 'Maximum number of times the ad creative may be served to a single unique user within the defined frequency cap period. Controls ad exposure and prevents overexposure to individual users.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.frequency_cap_period IS 'Time window over which the frequency cap impressions limit applies. Defines the reset interval for the per-user impression count (e.g., no more than 3 impressions per day).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.geo_targeting IS 'Geographic targeting parameters applied to this trafficking instruction, specifying the countries, regions, DMAs, or cities where the ad should be served. Expressed as a structured targeting string or comma-separated location codes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.impression_tracking_pixel_url IS 'URL of the impression tracking pixel fired upon each ad impression to record delivery counts. Used for third-party verification, billing reconciliation, and campaign measurement. May include multiple pixels concatenated or the primary pixel URL.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.instruction_number IS 'Externally-known, human-readable reference number for this trafficking instruction, used in communications with ad servers, media vendors, and internal trafficking teams. Typically follows a structured naming convention (e.g., TI-2024-00123).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.instruction_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the trafficking instruction: pending (created but not yet dispatched), sent (transmitted to ad server or vendor), confirmed (acknowledged by recipient), rejected (refused by recipient), or cancelled (voided before confirmation).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.instruction_type IS 'Classifies the nature of the trafficking instruction: new (initial dispatch of a creative), revision (update to an existing instruction), cancellation (termination of delivery), pause (temporary halt), or resume (restart after pause).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional operational notes, special instructions, or contextual information relevant to this trafficking instruction. Used by ad operations teams to communicate nuances not captured in structured fields.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.rejection_reason IS 'Free-text description of the reason provided by the ad server or media vendor when a trafficking instruction is rejected. Populated only when instruction_status is ''rejected''. Used for troubleshooting and resubmission workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.revision_number IS 'Sequential version number of this trafficking instruction, incremented each time a revision instruction is issued for the same placement and creative combination. Version 1 represents the original instruction.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.sent_timestamp IS 'Precise date and time when the trafficking instruction was transmitted to the ad server or media vendor. Used for SLA tracking, audit trails, and delivery timeline analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.third_party_verification_required IS 'Indicates whether third-party ad verification (e.g., DoubleVerify, Integral Ad Science) is mandated for this trafficking instruction per client or campaign requirements. When true, verification tags must be included in the ad serving setup.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.trafficking_date IS 'The date on which the trafficking instruction was formally issued and dispatched to the ad server or media vendor. Represents the principal real-world business event date for this operational record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.vast_tag_url IS 'The Video Ad Serving Template (VAST) tag URL used for video creative delivery. Provides the ad server with the XML-based instructions for serving video ads, including media file location, tracking events, and companion ads. Applicable for video placements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.viewability_tag_url IS 'URL of the viewability measurement tag embedded in the ad creative to track whether the ad was viewable per MRC and IAB viewability standards (e.g., 50% of pixels in view for 1 continuous second for display). Used for viewability reporting and vendor compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.vpaid_tag_url IS 'The Video Player-Ad Interface Definition (VPAID) tag URL enabling interactive video ad execution within the video player environment. Used for rich interactive video creatives requiring player-level communication. Applicable for VPAID-enabled placements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.trafficking_instruction.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.ad_channel IS 'Master reference entity for all media and distribution channels through which advertising is delivered — including paid search (SEM/PPC), social, display, video, email, SEO, OOH/DOOH, CTV/OTT, and programmatic. Owns the authoritative channel taxonomy with IAB-aligned classifications, channel codes, and delivery modalities. Also owns platform-specific operational configuration including DSP seat settings (The Trade Desk), UTM parameter conventions, bid strategy defaults, frequency cap policies, brand safety keyword lists, and GDPR/CCPA consent signal handling. SSOT for channel identity, taxonomy, and operational configuration across the enterprise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.ad_channel_id IS 'Unique identifier for the advertising channel. Primary key for the ad_channel entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Each ad channel (TV, digital, OOH, radio) maps to a specific GL account for revenue and cost classification in financial statements. This channel-to-GL mapping is standard chart-of-accounts configurat LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.taxonomy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.taxonomy. Business justification: Ad channel taxonomy standard selection: media planners must know which audience taxonomy standard (IAB, Nielsen, Comscore) a channel supports to correctly map audience segments for targeting activatio LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.taxonomy.taxonomy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Ad channels reference platform_name and dsp_seat_code as plain text. Linking to tech_partner normalizes the platform vendor relationship, enabling channel-level tech fee management, platform SLA track';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.agency_commission_pct IS 'Standard agency commission percentage applied to gross media spend on this channel. Typically 15% for traditional media, 10-15% for digital. Null if commission varies by client or IO.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.api_endpoint_url IS 'Base URL for the channels API integration. Used by ETL processes to retrieve campaign performance data, update bids, and sync creative assets. Confidential system configuration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.api_version IS 'Version of the API specification currently in use for this channel (e.g., v14, 2023-Q4). Critical for maintaining integration compatibility during platform upgrades.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.attribution_window_days IS 'Number of days after an ad interaction (click or view) during which conversions are attributed to this channel. Standard windows are 1, 7, 30, or 90 days depending on channel and business model.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.bid_strategy_default IS 'Default bidding strategy applied to campaigns on this channel unless overridden at campaign level. Determines how the platform optimizes bids to achieve campaign objectives. Code set: ref.bid_strategy_default.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.brand_safety_keywords IS 'Comma-separated list of keywords or content categories to exclude for brand safety (e.g., violence, adult content, controversial topics). Applied as negative targeting across all campaigns on this channel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.brand_safety_tier IS 'Default brand safety filtering level applied to inventory on this channel. Standard allows broad reach; strict applies maximum content exclusions to protect brand reputation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.ccpa_opt_out_supported IS 'Indicates whether this channel supports CCPA Do Not Sell signals for California users. Required for compliance with California privacy regulations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.channel_code IS 'Short alphanumeric code uniquely identifying the channel across all systems (e.g., SEM_GOOGLE, SOCIAL_FB, DISPLAY_PROG). Used as the business identifier in campaign planning, trafficking, and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.channel_name IS 'Human-readable name of the advertising channel (e.g., Google Search, Facebook Social, Programmatic Display).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.channel_status IS 'Current operational status of the channel. Active channels are available for campaign planning and buying; deprecated channels are phased out but may have historical data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.channel_type IS 'Primary classification of the channel by media type. Aligns with IAB taxonomy for cross-platform reporting and planning. Code set: ref.channel_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.click_attribution_window_days IS 'Number of days after a click during which conversions are attributed to this channel. Typically longer than view attribution window due to higher intent signal.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.consent_signal_format IS 'Format of privacy consent signals passed to this channel. TCF v2 (Transparency and Consent Framework) for GDPR, US Privacy String for CCPA, GPP (Global Privacy Platform) for multi-jurisdiction compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.currency_code IS 'Default currency for financial transactions on this channel. Three-letter ISO 4217 code (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP). Used for rate cards, billing, and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.delivery_modality IS 'Method by which media is bought and delivered through this channel. Determines operational workflow, trafficking requirements, and reconciliation processes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.dsp_seat_code IS 'Unique seat identifier within the DSP platform (e.g., The Trade Desk seat ID). Used for programmatic bid requests, deal configuration, and reconciliation. Confidential operational credential.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.effective_date IS 'Date when this channel configuration became active and available for campaign planning and buying. Used for historical tracking of channel availability.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.expiration_date IS 'Date when this channel configuration expires or was deprecated. Null for active channels. Used to track channel lifecycle and prevent planning on sunset channels.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.frequency_cap_default IS 'Default maximum number of times an ad can be shown to the same user within the frequency cap period. Prevents ad fatigue and optimizes reach. Null indicates no default cap.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.frequency_cap_period_default IS 'Time window over which the default frequency cap is applied (e.g., 3 impressions per day). Works in conjunction with frequency_cap_default.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.gdpr_consent_required IS 'Indicates whether GDPR consent signals must be passed for users in EU/EEA jurisdictions when serving ads on this channel. True for channels operating in or targeting European markets.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.notes IS 'Free-text field for operational notes, special instructions, or configuration details specific to this channel. Used by media planners and buyers for reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.platform_type IS 'Classification of the underlying technology platform. DSP (Demand-Side Platform) for programmatic buying, SSP (Supply-Side Platform) for inventory supply, or direct publisher platforms. Code set: ref.platform_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.pricing_model IS 'Default pricing model for media buys on this channel. CPM (Cost Per Mille) for impressions, CPC (Cost Per Click), CPA (Cost Per Acquisition), CPV (Cost Per View), CPCV (Cost Per Completed View), or flat fee. Code set: ref.pricing_model.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.supports_audience_targeting IS 'Indicates whether this channel supports audience segment targeting using first-party, third-party, or platform-native audience data. Critical for personalized campaign strategies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.supports_dayparting IS 'Indicates whether this channel supports daypart scheduling (time-of-day and day-of-week targeting). Common in broadcast, CTV, and digital channels for optimizing reach and frequency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.supports_geo_targeting IS 'Indicates whether this channel supports geographic targeting by country, region, DMA (Designated Market Area), postal code, or radius. Essential for local and regional campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.supports_programmatic IS 'Indicates whether this channel supports programmatic buying via DSP platforms and RTB (Real-Time Bidding) protocols. True for most digital channels; false for traditional media.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.utm_medium_default IS 'Default value for utm_medium parameter in campaign tracking URLs for this channel (e.g., cpc, social, display). Enables consistent channel attribution in web analytics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.utm_source_default IS 'Default value for utm_source parameter in campaign tracking URLs for this channel. Standardizes attribution and analytics reporting across Google Analytics and other web analytics platforms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.view_attribution_window_days IS 'Number of days after an ad view (impression without click) during which conversions are attributed to this channel. Typically 1-7 days for display and video channels.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.viewability_standard IS 'Viewability measurement standard applied to this channel. MRC (Media Rating Council) standard requires 50% of pixels in view for 1 second (display) or 2 seconds (video).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.viewability_threshold_pct IS 'Minimum viewability percentage required for impressions on this channel to be considered valid for billing and reporting purposes. Typically 50-70% based on MRC standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_channel.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.ad_format IS 'Reference catalog of all standardized advertising formats, their creative specifications, and trafficking requirements across channels — including IAB standard display units, video formats (VAST/VPAID), native, audio, OOH/DOOH specs, CTV interstitials, and rich media. Owns format dimensions, file size limits, MIME types, accepted creative file formats, click-through URL structures, impression tracking pixel requirements, viewability measurement vendor compatibility, platform-specific tagging requirements (Google Campaign Manager 360, The Trade Desk), IAB format classification codes, and channel×format trafficking matrices defining which specifications apply per channel context. SSOT for format identity, creative delivery specifications, and trafficking requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.ad_format_id IS 'Unique identifier for the advertising format. Primary key for the ad_format product.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.accepted_file_formats IS 'Comma-separated list of accepted file extensions for creative assets (e.g., JPG, PNG, GIF, MP4, MOV, HTML5, ZIP). Used for creative validation and trafficking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.accepted_mime_types IS 'Comma-separated list of accepted MIME types for creative files (e.g., image/jpeg, image/png, video/mp4, application/javascript). Defines technical compatibility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.ad_server_platform_compatibility IS 'Comma-separated list of ad server platforms that support this format (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360, The Trade Desk, Sizmek, Flashtalking). Used for trafficking validation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.aspect_ratio IS 'Proportional relationship between width and height (e.g., 16:9, 4:3, 1:1). Critical for video and CTV formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.brand_safety_tier IS 'Brand safety classification tier for the format, indicating the level of content adjacency control and verification required (standard, enhanced, premium).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.channel_applicability IS 'Comma-separated list of media channels where this format is applicable (e.g., digital, broadcast, OOH, DOOH, CTV, OTT, print, social, programmatic). Defines channel-format trafficking matrix.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.click_through_url_required IS 'Indicates whether a click-through URL is mandatory for this ad format. True for most digital formats; false for awareness-only formats (e.g., some OOH).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.deprecation_date IS 'Date when the ad format was deprecated and scheduled for retirement. Null for active formats. Format: yyyy-MM-dd.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.device_type_compatibility IS 'Comma-separated list of device types compatible with this format (e.g., desktop, mobile, tablet, CTV, smart_speaker, digital_billboard). Used for targeting and trafficking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.duration_seconds IS 'Standard duration of the ad creative in seconds. Applicable to video, audio, and CTV/OTT formats. Null for static formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.effective_date IS 'Date when the ad format specification became effective and available for use in media planning and trafficking. Format: yyyy-MM-dd.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.environment_type IS 'Primary environment where the ad format is delivered (e.g., web, app, CTV, DOOH, print, broadcast, social). Aligns with media planning and buying strategies. Code set: ref.environment_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.format_category IS 'High-level classification of the ad format by media type. Aligns with channel taxonomy and media planning categories. Code set: ref.format_category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.format_code IS 'Standardized alphanumeric code uniquely identifying the ad format across systems (e.g., DISPLAY_300X250, VIDEO_PREROLL_15S). Used for trafficking and system integration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.format_name IS 'Human-readable name of the advertising format (e.g., Medium Rectangle, Pre-Roll Video, Native In-Feed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.format_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the ad format. Active formats are available for trafficking; deprecated formats are phased out; retired formats are no longer supported.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.format_subcategory IS 'Detailed classification within the format category (e.g., banner, interstitial, pre-roll, mid-roll, post-roll, in-stream, out-stream, expandable, takeover).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.frequency_cap_recommended IS 'Recommended frequency cap (number of impressions per user per period) for this format to optimize user experience and campaign performance. Null if no recommendation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.height_pixels IS 'Standard height dimension of the ad creative in pixels. Null for non-display formats (e.g., audio, print).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.iab_format_code IS 'Official IAB classification code for the ad format, enabling standardized reporting and cross-platform compatibility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.impression_tracking_pixel_required IS 'Indicates whether an impression tracking pixel is required for delivery measurement. True for most digital formats to enable campaign reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.is_native_format IS 'Indicates whether the ad format is a native advertising format designed to match the form and function of the surrounding content. True for native in-feed, content recommendation, and sponsored content formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.is_programmatic_eligible IS 'Indicates whether the ad format is eligible for programmatic buying via Demand-Side Platforms (DSP) and Real-Time Bidding (RTB). True for formats supported by programmatic infrastructure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.max_file_size_kb IS 'Maximum allowed file size for the creative asset in kilobytes. Enforced during creative upload and trafficking validation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.placement_position_options IS 'Comma-separated list of allowed placement positions for this format (e.g., above_the_fold, below_the_fold, in_feed, interstitial, pre_roll, mid_roll, post_roll, sidebar, footer). Used for trafficking and optimization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.retirement_date IS 'Date when the ad format was fully retired and removed from active use. Null for active and deprecated formats. Format: yyyy-MM-dd.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.supports_animation IS 'Indicates whether the ad format supports animated creative content (e.g., GIF, HTML5 animation, video). False for static-only formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.supports_audio IS 'Indicates whether the ad format supports audio playback. True for video, audio, and CTV/OTT formats; false for display and print.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.supports_interactivity IS 'Indicates whether the ad format supports interactive elements (e.g., expandable units, rich media, VPAID). True for formats allowing user engagement beyond click-through.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.trafficking_notes IS 'Free-text field capturing special trafficking instructions, technical requirements, or operational notes for this ad format. Used by trafficking teams during campaign setup.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.vast_version_supported IS 'Supported VAST specification version for video ad serving (e.g., 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 4.1, 4.2). Null for non-video formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.viewability_measurement_supported IS 'Indicates whether the ad format supports viewability measurement per Media Rating Council (MRC) standards. True for formats compatible with viewability vendors.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.viewability_vendor_compatibility IS 'Comma-separated list of viewability measurement vendors compatible with this format (e.g., IAS, MOAT, DoubleVerify, Comscore). Used for third-party verification setup.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.vpaid_version_supported IS 'Supported VPAID specification version for interactive video ads (e.g., 1.0, 2.0). Null for non-interactive or non-video formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.width_pixels IS 'Standard width dimension of the ad creative in pixels. Null for non-display formats (e.g., audio, print).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.ad_format.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.placement IS 'Defines specific ad placement positions within a publisher property and channel — e.g., homepage leaderboard, in-stream pre-roll, sidebar rectangle, sponsored post slot, or DOOH screen location. Captures placement-level attributes including position type, above/below-fold classification, viewability rate benchmarks, CPM floor pricing, audience reach, and platform-specific trafficking requirements for Google Campaign Manager 360 and The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.placement_id IS 'Primary key for placement';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: A placement position is defined within a specific advertising channel (display, video, social, OOH, etc.). The channel determines the technical specifications, trafficking requirements, and pricing mo';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.publisher_property_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.publisher_property. Business justification: A placement position (e.g., homepage leaderboard, pre-roll slot) is physically located within a specific publisher property. This is the fundamental parent-child relationship: placement belongs to pub';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.ad_format_id IS 'Default ad format sold in this placement position.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.placement_code IS 'Business code uniquely identifying the placement position across ad server and DSP setups.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.placement_name IS 'Human-readable placement position name (e.g. Homepage Leaderboard 728x90).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.position_type IS 'Position type of the placement within the property.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.fold_position IS 'Above or below the fold classification for display placements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.viewability_rate_benchmark_pct IS 'Historical MRC viewability rate benchmark for this placement (0-100).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.cpm_floor_price IS 'Minimum CPM accepted for this placement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.floor_price_currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 currency of the CPM floor price.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.estimated_monthly_reach IS 'Estimated monthly unique audience reach of the placement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.cm360_placement_code IS 'Placement identifier in Google Campaign Manager 360.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.ttd_inventory_code IS 'Inventory/placement identifier in The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.trafficking_requirements IS 'Platform-specific trafficking requirements (tags';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.placement_status IS 'Lifecycle status of the placement position.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.placement.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE media.publisher_property IS 'Represents individual media properties, sites, apps, networks, or placements owned or operated by a publisher — e.g., a specific website, mobile app, TV network, OOH billboard network, or streaming channel. Captures property-level attributes including URL/app ID, content vertical, audience composition, MRC-audited traffic certification, viewability benchmarks, and brand safety classification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.publisher_property_id IS 'Unique identifier for the publisher property. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: A publisher property operates within a primary advertising channel (e.g., a website is a display/digital channel property, a TV network is a broadcast channel property, a podcast is an audio channel p';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.primary_audience_segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Publisher audience profiling: media planners select inventory based on publisher audience composition. The denormalized `audience_composition` text field should be replaced with a proper FK to the aud LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.publisher_id IS 'Reference to the publisher or media owner that operates this property.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.taxonomy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.taxonomy. Business justification: Inventory taxonomy classification: publisher properties are classified using audience taxonomy standards (IAB content categories) for targeting eligibility and audience-to-inventory matching. The deno LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.taxonomy.taxonomy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.ad_fraud_risk_score IS 'The fraud risk score for this property (0-100 scale, where higher scores indicate higher fraud risk) based on invalid traffic (IVT) detection and TAG certification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.ad_server_platform IS 'The primary ad serving platform used by this property (e.g., Google Ad Manager, Freewheel, Xandr, Magnite).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.app_bundle_code IS 'The platform-specific bundle identifier for mobile or CTV apps (e.g., com.example.app).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.app_store_code IS 'The unique identifier for the mobile or CTV app in the app store (e.g., Apple App Store ID, Google Play Store ID, Roku Channel Store ID).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.average_cpm IS 'The average Cost Per Mille (CPM) rate achieved for ad placements on this property over the past 90 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.brand_safety_classification IS 'The brand safety tier or classification for this property based on content quality, adjacency risk, and third-party verification (e.g., TAG Certified, IAS/DV brand safety scores).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.campaign_manager_site_code IS 'The unique site identifier for this property in Google Campaign Manager 360 ad serving platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.content_vertical IS 'The primary content category or vertical of the property (e.g., News, Sports, Entertainment, Finance, Lifestyle) per IAB Content Taxonomy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.country_code IS 'The primary country where this property operates, using ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code (e.g., USA, GBR, CAN).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.currency_code IS 'The currency used for pricing and billing for this property, using ISO 4217 three-letter currency code (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.floor_cpm IS 'The minimum Cost Per Mille (CPM) rate accepted for ad placements on this property.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.geographic_coverage IS 'The primary geographic markets or regions served by this property (e.g., ''USA National'', ''New York DMA'', ''EMEA'', ''Global'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.language_code IS 'The primary language of content on this property, using ISO 639-1 two-letter language code (e.g., en, es, fr).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.monthly_impressions IS 'The average number of ad impressions available per month for this property.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.monthly_unique_visitors IS 'The average number of unique visitors or users per month for this property.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.mrc_accredited IS 'Indicates whether the property''s traffic and audience measurement has been audited and accredited by the Media Rating Council (MRC).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.mrc_audit_date IS 'The date of the most recent MRC audit or certification for this property.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.pmp_deals_available IS 'Indicates whether this property offers Private Marketplace (PMP) programmatic deals with negotiated terms and pricing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.prisma_property_code IS 'The unique identifier for this property in the Mediaocean Prisma media planning and buying system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.programmatic_enabled IS 'Indicates whether this property is available for programmatic buying through Demand-Side Platforms (DSPs) and Supply-Side Platforms (SSPs).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.property_code IS 'The externally-known unique identifier or code for this property used in media planning and buying systems (e.g., site ID, app ID, network code).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.property_name IS 'The human-readable name of the media property, site, app, network, or placement (e.g., ''ESPN Mobile App'', ''The New York Times Homepage'', ''Clear Channel Billboard Network'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.property_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the property in the media inventory system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.property_type IS 'The category of media property: website, mobile app, Connected TV (CTV) app, streaming channel, TV network, radio station, Out-of-Home (OOH) network, or print publication. Code set: ref.property_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.property_url IS 'The primary URL or web address for the property (for websites and web-based properties).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.rtb_enabled IS 'Indicates whether this property supports Real-Time Bidding (RTB) for ad inventory.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.supported_ad_formats IS 'Comma-separated list of ad formats supported by this property (e.g., display, video, native, audio, DOOH).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.tag_certified IS 'Indicates whether the property is certified by the Trustworthy Accountability Group (TAG) for brand safety and anti-fraud measures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.vast_version IS 'The version of the Video Ad Serving Template (VAST) standard supported by this property (e.g., VAST 2.0, VAST 3.0, VAST 4.0).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.video_player_type IS 'The type of video player used on this property for video ad serving (e.g., JW Player, Brightcove, Video.js, native CTV player).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.viewability_benchmark_pct IS 'The average viewability rate for ad placements on this property, measured as percentage of impressions that meet MRC viewability standards (50% of pixels in view for 1+ seconds for display, 2+ seconds for video).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.vpaid_supported IS 'Indicates whether this property supports the Video Player-Ad Interface Definition (VPAID) standard for interactive video ads.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN media.publisher_property.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE vendor.accreditation IS 'Tracks formal accreditation, certification, and compliance status records for vendors — including TAG Brand Safety Certified, TAG Certified Against Fraud, MRC accreditation, IAB Gold Standard, and ASA/FTC compliance certifications. Each record captures the certifying body, certification type, issue date, expiry date, certificate reference number, and current validity status. Enables brand safety and supply chain transparency enforcement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.accreditation_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for each vendor accreditation, certification, or compliance record within the vendor domain SSOT.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the vendor (media publisher, technology partner, DSP, SSP, DMP, CDP, or production supplier) that holds this accreditation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.accreditation_status IS 'Current validity status of the accreditation record. ''active'' indicates the certification is current and enforceable; ''expired'' indicates the certification period has lapsed; ''suspended'' indicates temporary hold pending review; ''revoked'' indicates the certifying body has withdrawn the certification; ''pending'' indicates an application in progress.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.accreditation_tier IS 'The tier or level of the accreditation where the certifying body defines multiple levels (e.g., IAB Gold Standard tiers, MRC provisional vs. full accreditation). Supports vendor segmentation and preferential buying decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.anti_fraud_certified IS 'Indicates whether this accreditation record confers TAG Certified Against Fraud status on the vendor. True when the certification type is TAG Certified Against Fraud and status is active. Supports invalid traffic (IVT) mitigation in programmatic buying.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.application_date IS 'The date on which the vendor first submitted the application for this accreditation or certification. Supports onboarding workflow tracking and time-to-accreditation analytics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.audit_cycle IS 'The frequency at which the certifying body requires the vendor to undergo re-audit or re-assessment to maintain the accreditation (e.g., annual TAG re-certification, biennial MRC audit). Drives renewal workflow scheduling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.brand_safety_certified IS 'Indicates whether this accreditation record confers TAG Brand Safety Certified status on the vendor. True when the certification type is TAG Brand Safety Certified and status is active. Enables rapid brand safety filtering in media buying workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.ccpa_compliant IS 'Indicates whether the vendor has demonstrated CCPA compliance as part of this accreditation record. Relevant for US-based audience data operations, programmatic buying, and DMP/CDP integrations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.certificate_reference_number IS 'The official certificate or registration number issued by the certifying body (e.g., TAG seal ID, MRC accreditation number, IAB Gold Standard reference). Used for external verification and audit trail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.certification_name IS 'The full official name of the certification or accreditation program as designated by the certifying body (e.g., ''TAG Brand Safety Certified Seal'', ''MRC Digital Audience-Based Buying Accreditation''). Provides human-readable identification beyond the type code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.certification_type IS 'The specific type of accreditation or certification held by the vendor. Covers brand safety, anti-fraud, audience measurement, content standards, and regulatory compliance certifications. Code set: ref.certification_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.certifying_body IS 'The governing or standards body that issued the accreditation or certification (e.g., TAG, MRC, IAB, ASA, FTC). Determines the authority and scope of the certification. Code set: ref.certifying_body.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.certifying_body_contact IS 'Name or email of the primary contact at the certifying body responsible for managing this accreditation record. Used for renewal correspondence and audit coordination.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.channel_scope IS 'The advertising channel(s) covered by this accreditation (e.g., programmatic display, OTT/CTV, DOOH). Aligns with IAB channel taxonomy and supports media buying compliance checks. Code set: ref.channel_scope.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.expiry_date IS 'The date on which the accreditation or certification expires and must be renewed. Null for certifications with no defined expiry. Critical for brand safety enforcement and supply chain transparency checks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.fee_usd IS 'The fee paid by the vendor to the certifying body to obtain or renew this accreditation, denominated in US Dollars. Supports vendor cost tracking, budget management, and P&L reconciliation for supply chain compliance expenditure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.gdpr_compliant IS 'Indicates whether the vendor has demonstrated GDPR compliance as part of this accreditation record. Relevant for European media buying, data processing agreements, and audience targeting operations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.geography_scope IS 'ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code(s) indicating the geographic markets covered by this accreditation (e.g., ''USA'', ''GBR|DEU|FRA''). Pipe-delimited for multi-country scope. Supports GDPR, CCPA, and regional compliance enforcement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.iab_gold_standard IS 'Indicates whether the vendor holds IAB Gold Standard certification as part of this accreditation record. Covers ads.txt/sellers.json adoption, brand safety, and anti-fraud commitments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.issue_date IS 'The date on which the certifying body formally issued or granted the accreditation to the vendor. Marks the start of the certification''s validity period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.last_audit_date IS 'The date of the most recent audit or assessment conducted by the certifying body against this accreditation. Used to assess currency of compliance and schedule next audit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.mrc_accredited IS 'Indicates whether this accreditation record reflects MRC accreditation for audience measurement or ad verification. True when certifying_body is MRC and status is active. Supports Nielsen/Comscore measurement validation and media buying quality assurance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.next_audit_date IS 'The scheduled date for the next audit or re-assessment by the certifying body. Supports proactive compliance management and vendor onboarding risk assessment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional context, conditions, or observations related to this accreditation record (e.g., conditional approval notes, scope limitations, certifying body commentary). Supports operational transparency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.reinstatement_date IS 'The date on which a previously suspended or revoked accreditation was reinstated by the certifying body. Supports vendor lifecycle management and historical compliance audit trails.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.renewal_alert_days IS 'Number of days before expiry_date at which automated renewal alerts should be triggered for this accreditation. Configurable per certification type to support proactive compliance management (e.g., 90 days for TAG, 60 days for MRC).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.renewal_date IS 'The date on which the vendor submitted or completed the renewal application for this accreditation. Distinct from expiry_date; tracks the renewal action rather than the deadline.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.scope_description IS 'Narrative description of the scope of the accreditation, including which services, channels, geographies, or business units are covered (e.g., ''Programmatic display and video buying via DSP'', ''Digital audience measurement for desktop and mobile''). Enables precise brand safety and supply chain enforcement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.supporting_document_url IS 'URL pointing to the official certificate document, audit report, or compliance evidence stored in the DAM (Digital Asset Management) system or secure document repository. Enables direct access to certification evidence for brand safety audits.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.suspension_date IS 'The date on which the certifying body suspended or revoked this accreditation. Populated only when accreditation_status is ''suspended'' or ''revoked''. Enables point-in-time compliance reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.suspension_reason IS 'Narrative explanation of why the accreditation was suspended or revoked by the certifying body. Populated only when accreditation_status is ''suspended'' or ''revoked''. Supports vendor risk management and supply chain transparency reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.accreditation.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE vendor.publisher IS 'Master record for media publishers and inventory owners — including digital publishers, broadcast networks, OOH operators, DOOH networks, CTV/OTT platforms, and print media owners. Captures publisher profile, IAB content category classifications, audience reach, MRC-audited measurement status, brand safety tier, and supply path transparency (SPO) attributes. Distinct from DSP/SSP technology partners.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.publisher_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the publisher record in the vendor domain master. Primary key for all downstream joins and lineage tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.accreditation_id IS 'Unique TAG-issued certification identifier for the publisher. Used to verify certification status via the TAG registry and to validate supply chain transparency in programmatic buying workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.parent_publisher_id IS 'Self-referencing identifier pointing to the parent publisher entity, enabling hierarchical modelling of publisher groups and media conglomerates (e.g., a local TV station under a national broadcast network). Null for top-level publishers.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Publisher is a specialized subtype of supplier (media publishers and inventory owners). This FK establishes the subtype-to-supertype relationship, allowing publisher to inherit common supplier master';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.ads_txt_verified IS 'Indicates whether the publisher''s ads.txt file has been validated, confirming that authorized digital sellers are declared and reducing the risk of unauthorized inventory reselling. Critical for supply path optimization (SPO) and programmatic fraud prevention.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.audience_measurement_source IS 'Identifies the third-party audience measurement provider or methodology used to validate the publisher''s audience reach figures. Determines the credibility and comparability of audience data for media planning and post-campaign reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.base_cpm_rate IS 'Publisher''s standard base CPM (Cost Per Mille) rate in the agency''s operating currency, representing the cost per 1,000 ad impressions. Serves as the benchmark rate for media planning, rate card negotiations, and budget estimation in Mediaocean Prisma. Classified as confidential commercial pricing data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.deal_type IS 'Primary deal structure type through which the publisher''s inventory is transacted. Determines buying workflow, pricing model, and IO/insertion order requirements in Mediaocean Prisma. Code set: ref.deal_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.grp_enabled IS 'Indicates whether the publisher supports Gross Rating Point (GRP) or Target Rating Point (TRP) based audience buying and reporting, typically applicable to broadcast, CTV/OTT, and premium digital video inventory. Enables GRP-based media planning in Nielsen Ad Intel integrated workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.iab_content_category_code IS 'Primary IAB Content Taxonomy category code (e.g., IAB1, IAB2-1) classifying the publisher''s editorial content vertical. Used for audience targeting, brand safety filtering, and contextual advertising alignment per IAB Content Taxonomy v3.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.inventory_type IS 'Primary ad inventory format type offered by the publisher. Drives format-specific buying workflows, creative specifications, and measurement methodologies. Code set: ref.inventory_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.last_review_date IS 'Date of the most recent periodic vendor review or Quarterly Business Review (QBR) conducted for this publisher, covering brand safety compliance, performance metrics, and accreditation status. Supports vendor governance and renewal workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.monthly_impressions IS 'Estimated or audited total monthly ad impression volume available from the publisher across all inventory types. Used for media planning capacity assessment, share of voice (SOV) calculations, and programmatic deal sizing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.monthly_unique_visitors IS 'Estimated or MRC-audited monthly unique visitor count for the publisher''s primary digital property, as reported by Comscore or Nielsen. Used for audience reach planning, CPM (Cost Per Mille) benchmarking, and media plan audience delivery estimation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.mrc_accreditation_scope IS 'Description of the specific measurement types and platforms covered under the publisher''s MRC accreditation (e.g., ''Display Impressions, Video Viewability, Cross-Platform''). Null if mrc_audited is false.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.next_review_date IS 'Scheduled date for the next periodic vendor review or accreditation renewal check for this publisher. Used to trigger compliance review workflows and ensure TAG/MRC certifications remain current.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.notes IS 'Free-text field for capturing additional operational notes, special buying conditions, negotiation history, or account management observations relevant to the publisher relationship. Used by media buying and account management teams.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.preferred_ssp IS 'Name of the publisher''s primary or preferred Supply-Side Platform (SSP) used for programmatic inventory monetization (e.g., Google Ad Manager, Magnite, PubMatic, Index Exchange). Used for supply path optimization (SPO) and deal activation in The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.programmatic_enabled IS 'Indicates whether the publisher''s inventory is available for programmatic buying via Demand-Side Platforms (DSPs) and Supply-Side Platforms (SSPs), including Real-Time Bidding (RTB) and private marketplace (PMP) deal structures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.publisher_type IS 'Classification of the publisher by inventory channel category. Distinguishes digital publishers, broadcast networks, Out-of-Home (OOH) operators, Digital Out-of-Home (DOOH) networks, Connected TV (CTV) / Over-the-Top (OTT) platforms, and print media owners. Drives channel-specific buying workflows and rate card application.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.rate_currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the publisher''s rate card pricing (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Ensures correct currency conversion and financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma billing workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.sellers_json_verified IS 'Indicates whether the publisher''s sellers.json file has been validated, providing transparency into the supply chain by identifying all entities authorized to sell the publisher''s inventory. Supports supply path optimization (SPO) and anti-fraud compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.spo_tier IS 'Supply Path Optimization (SPO) classification indicating the preferred supply path designation for this publisher. ''Direct'' = direct publisher relationship; ''Preferred'' = approved SSP path; ''Standard'' = open market; ''Excluded'' = removed from programmatic buying paths. Used by The Trade Desk and DSP buying teams to optimize supply chain efficiency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.vast_vpaid_support IS 'Indicates the publisher''s supported video ad serving standards: VAST (Video Ad Serving Template) only, VPAID (Video Player-Ad Interface Definition) only, both, or neither. Determines video creative compatibility and trafficking requirements in Google Campaign Manager 360.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.website_url IS 'Primary public-facing website URL of the publisher. Serves as the canonical digital identity reference for brand safety audits, supply path optimization (SPO) verification, and ads.txt/sellers.json validation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.publisher.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE vendor.supplier IS 'Canonical master record and Single Source of Truth (SSOT) for all third-party vendor identities in the advertising ecosystem. Encompasses media publishers (digital, broadcast, OOH, DOOH, CTV/OTT, print), technology platforms (DSPs, SSPs, DMPs, CDPs, ad servers, verification vendors such as IAS and DoubleVerify, attribution platforms, data providers), production houses, research providers, and supply chain partners. Captures legal entity details, vendor type classification (enum: publisher, tech_platform, production, research, other), IAB content category (for publishers), platform type per IAB Tech Lab taxonomy and API integration status (for tech partners), audience reach metrics, MRC-audited measurement status, TAG/MRC accreditation status, TAG Certified Against Fraud, brand safety tier rating, supply path transparency (SPO) attributes, diversity certification, data sharing agreement status, programmatic supply chain role, onboarding lifecycle state, and primary agency relationship owner. All other vendor-domain products reference this entity via supplier_id. Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma vendor records, Salesforce CRM, The Trade Desk, and Google CM360 integrations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.supplier_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the supplier record. Primary key for the vendor.supplier data product. All other vendor-domain products reference this entity via supplier_id. MASTER_PARTY role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.ads_txt_verified IS 'Indicates whether the publisher supplier''s authorized digital sellers (ads.txt) or sellers.json file has been verified by the agency''s programmatic operations team, confirming legitimate inventory authorization and reducing counterfeit inventory risk per IAB Tech Lab standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.agency_relationship_owner IS 'Name or identifier of the primary agency employee (e.g., media director, programmatic lead, or account director) responsible for managing the commercial relationship with this supplier. Used for accountability, QBR scheduling, and escalation routing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.api_integration_status IS 'Current status of the API integration between the agency''s technology stack and the supplier''s platform. Applicable primarily to tech_platform vendor types. Tracks whether automated data exchange (bid management, reporting, audience sync) is live, pending setup, inactive, or not applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.audience_reach IS 'Estimated total unique audience reach of the supplier''s media properties, expressed as number of unique users/devices per month. Sourced from Comscore or Nielsen Ad Intel measurement. Used in media planning for reach and frequency analysis and GRP/TRP calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.brand_safety_tier IS 'Agency-assigned brand safety tier rating for the supplier based on content quality, TAG certification, MRC accreditation, and supply chain transparency. Tier 1 = premium brand-safe inventory; Tier 2 = standard; Tier 3 = restricted/monitored; Unrated = pending assessment. Controls eligibility for client campaigns with brand safety mandates.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.cm360_vendor_code IS 'Unique vendor or site identifier assigned to the supplier within Google Campaign Manager 360 for ad trafficking, placement management, and delivery reporting. Enables reconciliation between CM360 delivery data and the vendor master.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.contract_expiry_date IS 'Expiry date of the master service agreement (MSA) or master vendor contract with the supplier. Triggers contract renewal workflows and controls whether new insertion orders (IOs) can be issued against this supplier in Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.country_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code representing the country where the supplier is legally incorporated. Drives regulatory compliance checks (GDPR, CCPA), tax treatment in SAP S/4HANA, and supply path transparency (SPO) reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code in which the supplier invoices the agency (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Used for multi-currency financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma billing workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.data_sharing_agreement IS 'Indicates whether a formal data sharing agreement is in place with the supplier, governing the exchange of audience data, campaign performance data, and measurement signals. Required for GDPR/CCPA compliance when audience data flows between the agency and the supplier.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.diversity_cert_type IS 'Specific type of diversity certification held by the supplier (e.g., MBE, WBE, LGBTBE, VOSB, SDVOSB, SBE). Populated only when diversity_certified is True. Used for granular diversity spend categorization and client reporting. Code set: ref.diversity_cert_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.diversity_certified IS 'Indicates whether the supplier holds a recognized diversity certification (e.g., MBE - Minority Business Enterprise, WBE - Women Business Enterprise, LGBTBE, VOSB). Supports client diversity spend reporting mandates and ANA supplier diversity program compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.iab_content_category IS 'IAB Content Taxonomy category code assigned to the publisher''s primary content vertical (e.g., IAB1 - Arts & Entertainment, IAB19 - Technology & Computing). Applicable to publisher vendor types. Used for brand safety targeting, contextual alignment, and programmatic supply curation in The Trade Desk and Google CM360.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.legal_name IS 'Full registered legal name of the supplier entity as filed with the relevant government authority. Used for contract execution, insertion orders (IOs), and financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.media_channel IS 'Primary media channel through which the publisher or supplier delivers advertising inventory. Applicable to publisher vendor types. Drives media planning and buying workflows in Mediaocean Prisma and The Trade Desk. Code set: ref.media_channel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.mediaocean_vendor_code IS 'Unique vendor identifier assigned within Mediaocean Prisma, the agency''s primary media planning, buying, and billing system of record. Used for cross-system reconciliation between the lakehouse silver layer and Mediaocean operational records.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.mrc_accredited IS 'Indicates whether the supplier''s audience measurement methodology or ad serving has been audited and accredited by the Media Rating Council (MRC). Critical for validating impression counting, viewability measurement, and GRP/TRP reporting integrity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.mrc_audit_date IS 'Date of the most recent MRC audit completion for the supplier''s measurement methodology or ad serving infrastructure. Used to assess currency of accreditation and trigger re-audit workflows when accreditation lapses.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.notes IS 'Free-text field for capturing supplementary information about the supplier that does not fit structured fields, such as special commercial terms, relationship history, escalation contacts, or onboarding exceptions noted by the agency relationship owner.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.onboarding_date IS 'Date on which the supplier was formally approved and activated in the agency''s vendor management system following completion of onboarding due diligence (financial, legal, brand safety, and compliance checks).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.onboarding_status IS 'Current state of the supplier in the agency onboarding and vendor management lifecycle. Controls whether the supplier is eligible for media buys, IO issuance, and payment processing in Mediaocean Prisma and SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.payment_terms IS 'Standard payment terms agreed with the supplier for invoice settlement, as configured in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma. Drives accounts payable scheduling and cash flow management in financial reconciliation workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.platform_type IS 'Specific platform classification per IAB Tech Lab taxonomy for tech_platform vendor types. Identifies the supplier''s role in the programmatic supply chain (e.g., DSP, SSP, DMP, CDP, ad server, verification vendor such as IAS/DoubleVerify, attribution platform, data provider). Null for non-tech-platform vendors. Code set: ref.platform_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.primary_contact_email IS 'Primary business email address for the supplier''s account representative or partnership contact. Used for IO delivery, billing correspondence, and campaign trafficking communications.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.primary_contact_name IS 'Full name of the primary business contact at the supplier organization responsible for account management, campaign trafficking, and billing inquiries.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.primary_contact_phone IS 'Primary business phone number for the supplier contact, formatted per ITU-T E.164 standard. Used for urgent campaign and billing escalations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.programmatic_supply_role IS 'Defines the supplier''s role in the programmatic supply chain as declared in ads.txt/sellers.json: direct (authorized direct seller of inventory), reseller (authorized to resell another seller''s inventory), both (acts as both), or not_applicable (non-programmatic supplier). Used for supply chain transparency and SPO analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.salesforce_account_code IS 'Unique account identifier for the supplier record in Salesforce CRM (Sales Cloud). Enables cross-system linkage between the vendor master and the CRM account for relationship management, contract tracking, and QBR reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.spo_enabled IS 'Indicates whether the supplier participates in the agency''s Supply Path Optimization (SPO) program, meaning the agency has a direct or preferred supply relationship with this vendor to reduce intermediary hops, improve transparency, and lower CPM costs in programmatic buying via The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.tag_certified_against_fraud IS 'Indicates whether the supplier holds current TAG Certified Against Fraud certification, a key brand safety and ad fraud prevention credential. Required for programmatic supply curation and brand safety tier assignment. Sourced from TAG registry.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.tag_seal_certification_code IS 'The unique TAG Seal identifier issued to the supplier upon achieving TAG certification (e.g., TAG Certified Against Fraud, TAG Brand Safety Certified). Used to verify certification authenticity via the TAG registry and enforce brand safety compliance in programmatic buying.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.tax_identifier IS 'Government-issued tax identification number (e.g., EIN in the US, VAT number in the EU) for the supplier''s legal entity. Required for W-9/W-8 compliance, SAP S/4HANA vendor master setup, and financial reconciliation in Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.trade_desk_partner_code IS 'Unique partner or supply partner identifier assigned to the supplier within The Trade Desk DSP platform. Used for programmatic buying configuration, bid management, and supply path optimization (SPO) tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.trading_name IS 'The brand or ''doing business as'' (DBA) name used in day-to-day media buying, campaign trafficking, and agency communications. May differ from the legal entity name.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.vendor_type IS 'Primary classification of the supplier within the advertising ecosystem. Drives downstream workflow routing, rate card applicability, and compliance checks. Enum: publisher (media owner), tech_platform (DSP/SSP/DMP/CDP/ad server/verification/attribution), production (creative/production house), research (audience/measurement provider), other.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.supplier.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE vendor.tech_partner IS 'Master record for advertising technology platform partners — DSPs, SSPs, DMPs, CDPs, ad servers, verification vendors (IAS, DoubleVerify), attribution platforms, and data providers. Captures platform type (IAB Tech Lab taxonomy), API integration status, data sharing agreements, TAG certification, and programmatic supply chain role. Supports The Trade Desk, Google CM360, and DMP/CDP integrations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.tech_partner_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the advertising technology platform partner record in the vendor master. Primary key for the tech_partner data product.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.accreditation_id IS 'Official TAG-issued certification identifier for the tech partner. Used to validate brand safety compliance and anti-fraud accreditation during programmatic deal setup and IO execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Tech_partner is a specialized subtype of supplier (advertising technology platform partners - DSPs, SSPs, DMPs, CDPs, ad servers, verification providers). This FK establishes the subtype-to-supertype';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.ads_txt_authorized IS 'Indicates whether the tech partner is listed as an authorized digital seller in the relevant ads.txt files, confirming legitimate inventory resale rights per IAB Tech Lab standards. Critical for anti-fraud and brand safety compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.annual_platform_fee IS 'Annual licensing or platform access fee payable to the tech partner, denominated in the contract currency. Used for budget planning, P&L reporting, and financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA FI/CO.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.api_endpoint_url IS 'Primary API endpoint URL for programmatic integration with the tech partner''s platform. Used by ETL pipelines and DSP/SSP connectors for bid requests, reporting pulls, and audience segment synchronization. Classified confidential as it represents proprietary integration infrastructure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.api_integration_status IS 'Current status of the API integration between the agency''s systems (The Trade Desk, Google CM360, Mediaocean Prisma) and the tech partner''s platform. Drives automated bid management, reporting ingestion, and audience sync workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.attribution_model_support IS 'Attribution modeling methodology supported by the tech partner''s platform for campaign performance measurement. Informs ROAS and CPA reporting configurations in Google CM360 and The Trade Desk. Code set: ref.attribution_model_support.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.audience_targeting_capability IS 'Indicates whether the tech partner provides audience targeting capabilities (e.g., DMP/CDP segment activation, lookalike modeling, contextual targeting). Relevant for DMP and CDP partners integrated with The Trade Desk audience management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.brand_safety_tier IS 'Internal brand safety tier assigned to the tech partner based on TAG certification, MRC accreditation, IAS/DoubleVerify verification scores, and supply chain transparency. Tier 1 = highest trust; Tier 3 = restricted use. Governs which client campaigns may activate this partner.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.contract_end_date IS 'Expiry date of the master service agreement or platform access contract with the tech partner. Nullable for evergreen agreements. Triggers renewal workflow in Workfront and SAP S/4HANA contract management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.contract_start_date IS 'Effective start date of the master service agreement or platform access contract with the tech partner. Used for contract lifecycle management in SAP S/4HANA PS and financial accrual scheduling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.data_residency_region IS 'Geographic region where the tech partner stores and processes data (e.g., EU, US, APAC). Critical for GDPR cross-border data transfer compliance (Standard Contractual Clauses) and CCPA jurisdiction assessments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.data_sharing_agreement_flag IS 'Indicates whether a formal data sharing agreement (DSA) is in place with the tech partner governing the exchange of audience data, campaign performance data, and first-party data. Required for DMP/CDP integrations under GDPR and CCPA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.data_sharing_agreement_ref IS 'Reference number or document identifier for the executed data sharing agreement with the tech partner. Links to the contract management system (SAP S/4HANA PS or Workfront DAM) for legal and compliance audit purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.fee_currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the annual platform fee and any transactional fees charged by the tech partner (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Required for multi-currency financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA FI.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.iab_tech_lab_member IS 'Indicates whether the tech partner is an active member of the IAB Tech Lab, which governs programmatic standards including OpenRTB, VAST, VPAID, and ads.txt. Membership status informs standards compliance expectations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.last_audit_date IS 'Date of the most recent vendor compliance audit conducted for the tech partner, covering TAG certification, MRC accreditation, GDPR DPA, and brand safety assessments. Supports annual vendor review cycles.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.measurement_capability IS 'Indicates whether the tech partner provides independent measurement, viewability verification, or attribution services (e.g., IAS, DoubleVerify, Nielsen, Comscore). Determines eligibility as a third-party measurement vendor on campaign IOs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.platform_type IS 'Categorical classification of the advertising technology platform per IAB Tech Lab taxonomy. Determines the partner''s role in the programmatic supply chain and which integration workflows apply. Code set: ref.platform_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.rtb_protocol_version IS 'OpenRTB protocol version supported by the tech partner for programmatic buying and selling (e.g., OpenRTB 2.5, OpenRTB 2.6, OpenRTB 3.0). Governs bid request/response schema compatibility with The Trade Desk and other DSP integrations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.sellers_json_verified IS 'Indicates whether the tech partner''s sellers.json file has been validated per IAB Tech Lab specification, confirming supply chain transparency for programmatic inventory. Required for SSP and ad exchange partners.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.soc2_certified IS 'Indicates whether the tech partner holds a current SOC 2 Type II certification, confirming security, availability, and confidentiality controls. Required for partners handling first-party audience data or campaign performance data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.supply_chain_role IS 'The partner''s functional role within the programmatic advertising supply chain as defined by IAB ads.txt and sellers.json standards. Supports supply chain transparency audits and brand safety compliance. Values: buyer (DSP), seller (SSP/publisher), intermediary (reseller), data_provider, measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.supported_channels IS 'Comma-separated list of advertising channels supported by the tech partner''s platform (e.g., Display, Video, CTV, OTT, DOOH, Audio, Native, Search). Informs media planning channel eligibility in Mediaocean Prisma and The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.tech_fee_rate IS 'Percentage-based technology fee charged by the partner per media dollar transacted through their platform (e.g., DSP tech fee as a percentage of media spend). Used in CPM/CPC rate card calculations and ROAS reporting in Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.vast_vpaid_support IS 'Supported video ad serving standard(s) for the tech partner''s platform. Determines compatibility with video campaign trafficking in Google CM360 and The Trade Desk. VAST 4.x is the current IAB Tech Lab standard; VPAID 2.0 is legacy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.tech_partner.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE vendor.vendor_rate_card IS 'Vendor-published rate card defining standard pricing for media inventory, production services, or technology platform fees. Captures rate card version, effective date range, currency, pricing model (CPM, CPC, CPA, flat fee, GRP-based), rate tiers by volume or audience segment, and negotiated vs. open-market rate flags. Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma rate card management and vendor IO terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.vendor_rate_card_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the vendor rate card record. Primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.advertiser_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.advertiser. Business justification: Negotiated rate cards in advertising are frequently specific to an advertiser (is_negotiated_rate flag exists). Agencies negotiate advertiser-specific pricing with publishers/suppliers; billing valida LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.source_system_rate_card_vendor_rate_card_id IS 'The native identifier of this rate card record in the originating source system (Mediaocean Prisma). Enables lineage tracing and reconciliation between the Silver Layer lakehouse and the operational system of record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the vendor (media publisher, technology partner, or production supplier) who issued this rate card.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.ad_format IS 'The specific creative ad format covered by this rate card entry (e.g., banner, video pre-roll, native, audio, rich media, interstitial). Aligns with IAB standard ad unit taxonomy and Google Campaign Manager 360 trafficking formats. Code set: ref.ad_format.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.ad_size IS 'The dimensions or specification of the ad unit covered by this rate (e.g., ''300x250'', ''728x90'', ''15s'', ''30s'', ''6s bumper''). Follows IAB standard ad unit sizes for display and video formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.added_value_description IS 'Free-text description of any added-value elements bundled with this rate card (e.g., bonus impressions, free creative production, data targeting inclusion, brand safety tools). Common in direct media deals and IO negotiations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.agency_commission_pct IS 'The standard agency commission percentage applicable to this rate card (typically 15% per 4As convention). Distinct from discount_rate_pct; represents the agency''s earned commission on media spend billed at this rate.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the internal stakeholder (media buyer, procurement manager) who approved this rate card for use. Supports internal governance and audit trail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.approved_date IS 'The date on which the rate card was internally approved by the media buying or procurement team for use in campaign planning and IO execution. Supports governance and audit trail requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.audience_segment_label IS 'The audience segment or demographic targeting profile for which this rate applies (e.g., ''Adults 18-34'', ''In-Market Auto Buyers'', ''Lookalike High-Value''). Supports audience-based rate differentiation used in DMP/CDP-driven buying on The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.base_rate IS 'The standard published rate for the pricing unit defined by the pricing_model (e.g., CPM rate in currency per 1,000 impressions, CPC rate per click, flat fee amount). This is the principal quantitative fact of the rate card before any volume discounts or negotiated adjustments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.brand_safety_tier IS 'The brand safety classification level associated with this rate card''s inventory. TAG (Trustworthy Accountability Group) certified inventory commands premium rates. Supports brand safety compliance and supply chain transparency requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.channel_category IS 'Broad channel classification for the media inventory covered by this rate card (e.g., digital, traditional broadcast/print, programmatic, direct-sold, out-of-home). Supports media planning and channel mix analytics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code in which the rate card rates are denominated (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Required for multi-currency media buying operations and financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.discount_rate_pct IS 'The percentage discount applied to the base_rate to arrive at the negotiated net rate (e.g., 15.00 for a 15% agency discount). Expressed as a percentage. Used in Mediaocean Prisma billing and SAP S/4HANA financial reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.effective_end_date IS 'The date after which this rate card version is no longer valid for new bookings. Nullable for open-ended rate cards with no defined expiry.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.effective_start_date IS 'The date from which this rate card version becomes binding and applicable for media buying, IO execution, and billing. Aligns with vendor IO terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.geo_market IS 'The geographic market or region for which this rate card applies (e.g., ''USA'', ''GBR'', ''New York DMA'', ''EMEA''). Rates may vary by market due to inventory supply and demand dynamics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.guaranteed_viewability_pct IS 'The minimum viewability percentage guaranteed by the vendor for inventory sold under this rate card (e.g., 70.00 for 70% viewability guarantee). Null if no viewability guarantee is offered. Supports campaign performance KPI tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.inventory_type IS 'The category of media inventory or service covered by this rate card. Classifies the supply type (e.g., display, video, OOH/Out-of-Home, DOOH/Digital Out-of-Home, OTT/Over-the-Top, CTV/Connected TV). Code set: ref.inventory_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.io_terms_reference IS 'Reference identifier or URL to the vendor''s standard Insertion Order (IO) terms and conditions document associated with this rate card. Links rate card pricing to contractual obligations in Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.is_negotiated_rate IS 'Indicates whether this rate is a negotiated/contracted rate (True) as opposed to the vendor''s published open-market rate (False). Negotiated rates are commercially sensitive and used in IO reconciliation and P&L reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.minimum_spend IS 'The minimum monetary commitment required by the vendor to activate this rate card or rate tier. Expressed in the currency defined by currency_code. Relevant for IO negotiation and budget planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional context, special conditions, or annotations related to this rate card entry (e.g., seasonal restrictions, exclusivity clauses, make-good provisions). Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma rate card comments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.placement_position IS 'The placement position or contextual location of the ad unit on the publisher''s inventory (e.g., above_the_fold, pre_roll, homepage_takeover). Position premiums are a standard component of vendor rate cards. Code set: ref.placement_position.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.pricing_model IS 'The commercial pricing model under which rates are defined. CPM (Cost Per Mille) for impression-based; CPC (Cost Per Click) for click-based; CPA (Cost Per Acquisition) for conversion-based; flat_fee for fixed-cost placements; GRP (Gross Rating Point) for broadcast/linear TV; CTV for Connected TV; CPCV for Cost Per Completed View. Code set: ref.pricing_model.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.published_date IS 'The date on which the vendor formally published or issued this rate card version. Distinct from effective_start_date; a rate card may be published in advance of its effective period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.rate_card_name IS 'Human-readable name or title of the rate card as published by the vendor (e.g., ''Q3 2024 Display Standard Rate Card'', ''Programmatic Open Market CPM Card'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.rate_card_number IS 'Externally-known alphanumeric identifier assigned by the vendor or Mediaocean Prisma to uniquely reference this rate card document. Used in Insertion Order (IO) negotiations and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.rate_card_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the rate card. ''active'' indicates the card is currently in use for media buying; ''superseded'' means a newer version has replaced it; ''expired'' means the effective period has lapsed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.rate_card_type IS 'Indicates whether the rates are open-market published rates or negotiated/contracted rates. ''programmatic_guaranteed'' and ''private_marketplace'' (PMP) reflect programmatic deal structures. Drives reconciliation logic in Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.rate_unit IS 'The unit of measure against which the base_rate is applied (e.g., per_mille for CPM, per_click for CPC, per_grp for GRP-based broadcast buying, flat for fixed-fee placements). Ensures correct billing calculation in Mediaocean Prisma. Code set: ref.rate_unit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.version IS 'Version identifier of the rate card (e.g., v1.0, v2.3). Tracks revisions issued by the vendor over time to support historical rate lookups and audit trails.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.viewability_standard IS 'The viewability measurement standard applied to inventory covered by this rate card (e.g., MRC display standard: 50% pixels for 1 second; MRC video: 50% pixels for 2 seconds). Affects rate premiums and campaign KPI commitments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.volume_threshold_max IS 'The upper bound of the volume or spend range that qualifies for this rate tier. Nullable for the highest open-ended tier. Used with volume_threshold_min to define tier eligibility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.volume_threshold_min IS 'The lower bound of the volume or spend range (in impressions, clicks, or currency units per currency_code) that qualifies for this rate tier. Used in conjunction with volume_threshold_max to define tier eligibility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.volume_threshold_unit IS 'The unit of measure for the volume thresholds (volume_threshold_min and volume_threshold_max). Specifies whether thresholds are in impressions, clicks, currency spend, GRP points, or other measurable units.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.volume_tier_label IS 'Human-readable label identifying the volume or spend tier this rate applies to (e.g., ''Tier 1: $0–$50K'', ''Tier 2: $50K–$250K'', ''Enterprise''). Supports tiered pricing structures common in programmatic and direct media deals.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.vendor_rate_card.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
